          "body": "The field first-syzygy gate is now reduced to an arbitrary basepoint-free pair, invariant under a common rational shift. For nonzero multiplier sections $v_0,v_1$, the translated-divisor supremum gives middle-window generation and the translated-divisor infimum gives the two-term kernel; basis coordinates then yield the full Koszul equality. Verified commits: `cca06250a`, `0b645cd57`, `0ff8f91a7`, `7d6eec25d`. The remaining field input is to identify the two `divFamPhi` coordinate sections as such a pair and discharge the four $H^1$ bounds."
