ver R_Z primes.\nGOTCHA (new, MEMORY-WORTHY): a term-level composition (Eq.trans of landed lemmas) elaborates fine under the tower, but any tactic forcing isDefEq/whnf on the giant relCurve types (e.g. rw to unfold chartReadMap, or a show) TIMES OUT even at 2000000 heartbeats. Keep step assembly as term-mode .trans / exact of pre-proven lemmas; avoid unfolding defs under the kappa(p) tower.\n\n=== KEYSTONE (VERBATIM; namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaGeneratorSeed; seed context vars {k}(C)(pi)... (hpi)(g r1 r2)(b1 b2)(i j); seedChartRing := DivCarveChartRing k (windowS_choice) (windowM_choice) g r1 r2 b1 b2 i j = R_Z) ===\nrelPinnedTermBaseChangeAlg_reading_windowEquiv (p : PrimeSpectrum R_Z)(b : Bool)(x : R_Z (X)[k] H0(windowM.F)) :\n  relPinnedTermBaseChangeAlg C R_Z kappa(p) pi b (1 (X) relThetaResSide (windowM_choice) b le_rfl (relThetaWindowEquiv C R_Z pi (windowM_choice) (relThetaPairH1_windowM) x))\n    = relThetaResSide (windowM_choice) b le_rfl (relThetaWindowEquiv C kappa(p) pi (windowM_choice) (relThetaPairH1_windowM) (windowCompare R_Z kappa(p) x))\nProof: (relPinnedTermBaseChangeAlg_one_tmul).trans (relPinnedSectionsMap_relThetaResSide_windowEquiv). This is I-0294 step 1 at the universal seed: f_V (X) kappa(p) moves to compared-window fibre readings.\n\n=== hinj_chart STATUS: NOT LANDED. The genuine XL wall = the section->functionField SUBMODULE germ bridge (UNBUILT, triple-confirmed) ===\nSteps 2 (ker(f_V(X)kappa(p)) <-> 2nd window via ker_baseChangeMkQ_eq_span_windowCompare + divUniversal_carve_residueField) and 3 (corank-g pin via finrank_divUniversalFibreKM_add + SlicingFlatKernel) BOTH require identifying the FIBRE READING IMAGE range(f_V (X) kappa(p)) \u2014 a kappa-subspace of the fibre CHART sections Gamma(V_kappa), read via relThetaResSide \u2014 with divUniversalFibreKM \u2014 a kappa-subspace of the fibre FUNCTION FIELD, read via divFamPhi/thetaFieldRead (divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span, Res:376). That relThetaResSide<->divFamPhi identification AT