      "body": "redesign brick 2 achiever BUILD COMPLETE \u2014 the relative achiever EXISTENCE landed (both keystones green, axiom-clean, committed). New file Picard/DivSchemeRedesignAchiever.lean (323 L), root-wired (HEAD-blob + only my import line after DivSchemeRedesignJFlat; sibling PicEtCrossBaseGraph and DivSchemeUnivFibreHinj working-tree root lines NOT swept). Single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake build GREEN under the mkdir lock (8758 jobs, my module 152s). Zero sorries, zero warnings in my file. Both keystones axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].\n\n=== THE ACHIEVER-LIFT OBSTRUCTION IS DISSOLVED (I-0258/0288) ===\nNot by a rigid reduction, but exactly as I-0289 predicted: the SURJECTION lift. divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span presents the fibre window as the K-span of the readings Phi(windowCompare R_Z K x); Scheme.exists_achiever_of_span (BaseDivisorSpan.lean \u2014 the ultrametric span-minimality keystone) locates an achiever AMONG the readings. So one relative seed section's fibre reading is a genuine achiever at z \u2014 I-0258's \"single window vector need not reduce to a CHOSEN f_p\" is true but irrelevant. No new base-change naturality square was needed; the span law carries the base change.\n\n=== LANDED KEYSTONES (VERBATIM \u2014 what the seedUniv revision consumes for sec z) ===\n\nCommit ab14a53d0 (general field K of the tower R_{I,J} -> R_Z -> K):\n- exists_achiever_relThetaWindowEquiv_mem_divUniversalSeedK\n    {A : (relCurve C K).CurveDivisor}\n    (hA : divUniversalFibreKM C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 i j K \u2264 Scheme.divisorSections K A \u22a4)\n    (hne : divUniversalFibreKM C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 i j K \u2260 \u22a5)\n    {z : relCurve C K} (hz : z \u2260 genericPoint (relCurve C K)) :\n    \u2203 x \u2208 (divUniversalFstWindow C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j).toSubmodule,\n      relThetaWindowEquiv C R_Z \u03c0 (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) x\n        \u2208 divUniversalSeedK C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j \u2227\n      windowCompare R_Z K x \u2260 0 \u2227\n      \u2203 hr : divFamPhi C K \u03c0 (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (windowCompare R_Z K x) \u2260 0,\n        coeffAt hz (A + Scheme.divOf (relCurve C K \u2198 Spec (CommRingCat.of K))\n            (Units.mk0 (divFamPhi C K \u03c0 (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (windowCompare R_Z K x)) hr))\n          = (Scheme.baseDivisorAt K (divUniversalFibreKM C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 i j K) A \u27e8z, hz\u27e9 : \u2124)\n  (R_Z = DivCarveChartRing k (windowS_choice\u2026\u2022fiberWeilDivisor \u03c0) (windowM_choice\u2026\u2022fiberWeilDivisor \u03c0) g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j.)\n\nCommit 4166521b9 (seed-prime instantiation at K := \u03ba(p), A := N \u2212 d_p \u2014 THE deliverable):\n- exists_relThetaWindowEquiv_mem_divUniversalSeedK_achieves_seedPrime\n    (hO : Sheaf.h0 (C.left.moduleKSheaf k) = 1)\n    (h\u03c7 : Sheaf.chi (C.left.moduleKSheaf k) = 1 - (g : \u2124))\n    (p : PrimeSpectrum R_Z)\n    (hne : divUniversalFibreKM C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 i j p.asIdeal.ResidueField \u2260 \u22a5)\n    {z : relCurve C p.asIdeal.ResidueField} (hz : z \u2260 genericPoint (relCurve C p.asIdeal.ResidueField)) :\n    \u2203 x \u2208 (divUniversalFstWindow C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j).toSubmodule,\n      relThetaWindowEquiv C R_Z \u03c0 (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) x\n        \u2208 divUniversalSeedK C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j \u2227\n      windowCompare R_Z p.asIdeal.ResidueField x \u2260 0 \u2227\n      \u2203 hr : divFamPhi C p.asIdeal.ResidueField \u03c0 (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g)\n          (windowCompare R_Z p.asIdeal.ResidueField x) \u2260 0,\n        coeffAt hz ((windowN C p.asIdeal.ResidueField h\u03c0 g\n              - divUniversalSeedFibreDivisor C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7 p)\n            + Scheme.divOf (relCurve C p.asIdeal.ResidueField \u2198 Spec (CommRingCat.of p.asIdeal.ResidueField))\n                (Units.mk0 (divFamPhi C p.asIdeal.ResidueField \u03c0 (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g)\n                    (windowCompare R_Z p.asIdeal.ResidueField x)) hr))\n          = (Scheme.baseDivisorAt p.asIdeal.ResidueField (divUniversalFibreKM C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 i j p.asIdeal.ResidueField)\n              (windowN C p.asIdeal.ResidueField h\u03c0 g - divUniversalSeedFibreDivisor C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7 p) \u27e8z, hz\u27e9 : \u2124)\n\n=== HOW THE seedUniv REVISION CONSUMES IT (sec z) ===\nsec z := relThetaWindowEquiv C R_Z \u03c0 (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (relThetaPairH1_windowM C \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) x, which lies in divUniversalSeedK (2nd component). It is BOTH:\n (a) fibrewise nonzero \u2014 windowCompare R_Z \u03ba(p) x \u2260 0 (3rd component) \u2014 feeds Brick 2 (exists_forall_windowCompare_ne_zero) -> Brick 3 (relPinnedSectionsMap_relThetaResSide_windowEquiv_ne_zero) -> the seed's hfib clause, EXACTLY as the old DivSchemeSeedUnivBridge sec did; AND\n (b) a RELATIVE ACHIEVER at z \u2014 its \u03ba(p)-fibre reading Phi(windowCompare R_Z \u03ba(p) x) cuts EXACTLY d_p: ((N \u2212 d_p) + div reading)_z = baseDivisorAt(divUniversalFibreKM)_z (4th component), i.e. minimal vanishing at z (ord = base-divisor order). z is NOT an extra zero. This is EXACTLY what the old windowCompare\u22600 sec LACKED (I-0288 fact 3); it discharges the I-0288 hle razor AT z.\nSo the revised seedUniv.sec = this x's window image, and the achiever equation is the new content the ann-based h z (brick 3) then extends across D(h z) by excluding the OTHER extra zeros.\n\n=== RESIDUAL (for the seedUniv-re