      "body": "DD-R SPEC LANDED (informal/spec-dd-r.md, commit 8c12b88cb) \u2014 the two gate ADJUDICATIONS decided, evidence file:line in the spec.\n\nVERDICT A (I-0186 item 2 x I-0182): the off-overlap normalization is mathematically UNAVAILABLE \u2014 P-fib's divisor is the modulus itself (existsUnique_effective_divisor_of_carve, RiemannRoch/PFib.lean:241, D := baseDivisor of the GIVEN window, :282, pinned pointwise by baseDivisorAt_normalization :127); as the Z(diamond)-point varies D ranges over ALL effective deg-g divisors including g*x for x in pi^-1(Gm); no translation/rescale exists. BUT DD-R consumes NEITHER hsurj NOR hdeg: the recover direction is pullback of a UNIVERSAL certified family built by local generators from the universal carve pair (worksheet 3.4.1) \u2014 divFamOfDivisor appears nowhere; the only degree identity needed is fibrewise FOR CARVE-CERTIFIED FAMILIES and closes MV-free by the certified-degree pinch (corank g [DD-4 Task 5] + SectionBound:248 => deg <= 2g + exact rank_normalization WindowLedger:396 => deg = g). I-0182's one-sided-dictionary route is SUPERSEDED for DD-R. The hsurj/overlap obstruction MIGRATES TO DAT-B's coverage row (binding boundary flag in spec 1); designed relief recorded: DD-R's field instance gives a window-route divFamOfDivisor for ALL D (certificate from the second window, no support separation) \u2014 I-0186 stages 3-5 potentially moot for DAT-B. hdeg stays the sole XL, UNFUNDED and UNCONSUMED. Fallback if DDR-4/DDR-8 wall: matrix-chart AMBER (worksheet 3.6(d)), NOT general MV (it would not unblock the relative bricks).\n\nVERDICT B (I-0159 trailing (ii)): CHART-LOCAL SUFFICES \u2014 glued grPoint : (T -> grOver) -> grFunctor value is NOT consumed by DD-R, stays deferred. Family->hom is the GRQ grPointOfRankQuotient pattern (GrassmannianQuot.lean:4984, functor-value->scheme-map gluing) on the LANDED chart kit: matrixPoint_factors_chart_iff (GrassmannianChartFrame.lean:271), chartTautologicalPoint (GrassmannianTautological.lean:110), GL-cocycle compat (GrassmannianTautologicalCocycle.lean:110) \u2014 note I-0159 trailing (i) AND (iii) are ALREADY LANDED. Hom->family pulls back the universal DIVISOR family; the gluing weight sits on the divisor side (DD-1(c) mapAlg + DD-1(e) vehicle + DD-2), needed anyway for divFunctor to be a functor (PicEtMap precedent) \u2014 grPoint would be pure duplication. Residual mandatory DD-3 work: ZERO. DD-R owns two S-M plumbing bricks (chart-locus cover + hom-ext).\n\nBRICKS (spec 4): DDR-1 carve locus/DivScheme/iota [L, launchable NOW] || DDR-7 hom-ext [S-M, NOW] -> DDR-3 local generators [L] -> DDR-4 certificate transport [L-XL, THE seam, Fable-held, probe-first] -> {DDR-2 degree pinch [S-M], DDR-5 eps-projection [M], DDR-6 classify [M-L]} -> DDR-8 relative mono [L] -> DDR-9 divRep assembly [M-L]. Gates: DD-4 Tasks 4-7 + base-field-transport seam gate DDR-2/5/6; DD-1(c) mapAlg + DD-2 gate only DDR-9 (divRepAff first if DD-2 trails). RISKIEST: DDR-4's bridge between DD-1's gluedSubmodule equalizer and the engine Cech H0 of the constructed glued sheaf (anti-circular route: fibrewise P-fib -> relTwistRigidEngine -> certificate; support tube licensed by standing IsProper C.hom). Trap recorded: fibrewise containment does NOT imply relative containment over nonreduced bases (k[eps] counterexample) \u2014 all relative containments routed through colon-Tor or rank arithmetic.\n\nagent-ready",
