      "body": "DD-1c (f) INVERSE-LAW ADJUDICATION \u2014 VERDICT (2026-07-17, Opus prover). Follow-on to I-0179/I-0171/I-0167 (all KEPT OPEN as machinery maps). Commit d4d87e30, Picard/DivisorFamilyFieldEquiv.lean (214 lines, root-wired, own closure green 8644 jobs, keystones lean_verify axiom-clean [propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound]).\n\nWHAT LANDED (3 declarations):\n- Scheme.divEq_of_presentationDivisor_eq : the CONVERSE of the landed presentationDivisor_eq_of_divEq. Two LocalEquations on the curve with the SAME Weil divisor are DivEq. Proof: on the common refinement d1.cover \u2293 d2.cover, at each point x the ratio r = elem1 x / elem2 x has ordZ = 1 at every closed point z of the overlap (equal orders read the equal divisor coefficient off any piece: MeromorphicPresentation.ordZ_elem_eq + coeffAt_presentationDivisor + toAdd injective), so r and r-inv are both O(0)-sections (RiemannRoch.DivisorSheafZero.exists_section_germ_eq), i.e. r is a unit section (germ_injective_of_isIntegral) rescaling d2.eqn x to d1.eqn x. Gives the full characterization DivEq d1 d2 <-> presentationDivisor d1 = presentationDivisor d2.\n- divFamDivisor_injective : the forward map divFamDivisor is INJECTIVE on DivFam, UNCONDITIONALLY. Two families with equal divisor are DivEq (above), hence equal in the setoid.\n- divFamFieldEquivOfDegOfSurj : the equiv DivFam ~ {D // 0<=D and deg K D = n} assembled from two named hypotheses (sorry-free, conditional).\n\nTHE VERDICT (decides task 2 \u2014 outcome (b), NOT (a), NOT (c)-blanket): The SECOND inverse law divFamOfDivisor (divFamDivisor F) = F does NOT need general MV. It IS divFamDivisor_injective (landed): once the backward map exists, both sides of the law present the same divisor, so injectivity forces them equal. The full divFamFieldEquiv needs EXACTLY TWO further inputs, neither of which is the second law:\n  (1) hdeg = general-MV forward-degree deg(divFamDivisor F) = n for an ARBITRARY certified family. This is the honest Mayer-Vietoris wall of I-0179 (the separated identity deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated constrains finrank W(A'') of a FRESH separated adaptation, not finrank W(A) of F's own adaptation; connecting them = adaptation-independence of the glued rank = the XL). Needed even to LAND the forward map in the deg-n subtype. STILL UNFUNDED.\n  (2) hsurj = backward realization: every effective deg-n divisor is divFamDivisor of some certified family, via PointPresentation.pointEquations products + a support-separating adaptation. LARGE but needs NO general MV: the constructed adaptation is support-separated so its certificate rank finrank W = deg D = n comes FOR FREE from deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated with deg D = n an input hypothesis. This = task 1's backward map divFamOfDivisor + first inverse law divFamDivisor_divFamOfDivisor. NOT landed this session (multi-file construction: LocalEquations product realizing D, support-separated adaptation isolating support points in the two PINNED charts, finiteness of colengths, certificate (c1)-(c4); (c3)/(c4) free over field).\n\nFOR THE DD-R SPEC (consumes this dictionary): You do NOT need to fund the general-MV brick (1) if you consume the ONE-SIDED dictionary. If P-fib supplies a UNIQUE effective deg-n divisor D (its uniqueness), then hsurj's family for D feeds divFamOfDivisor and the one law divFamDivisor(family)=D round-trips through the divisor; because divFamDivisor is MONO (divFamDivisor_injective, landed), its section is determined, so the second inverse law is not separately required. Provided epsilon (DD-4) is mono, family equality is testable after epsilon. => DD-R can consume {backward map (hsurj, fundable) + divFamDivisor_injective (landed)} and skip general MV.\n\nNEXT LANE (to reach full equiv): build hsurj = the backward map divFamOfDivisor (task 1). Machinery: pointEquations (PointPresentation.lean:255) products via LocalEquations.mul (DivisorClass.lean:333) with presentationDivisor additivity; support-separated adaptation isolating each support point (refine exists_divisorAdaptation to make pieces contain <=1 support point); certificate via finrank_glued_eq_sum_of_separated + finrank_colength_eq_sum (finiteness of colength is the extra obligation), rankAtStalk=finrank over field, (c3)/(c4) trivial. Then plug divFamOfDivisor + first law into divFamFieldEquivOfDegOfSurj hdeg hsurj. hdeg (general MV) remains the sole XL.\n\nagent-ready\n\n=== UPDATE (2026-07-17, Opus hsurj prover \u2014 see follow-on I-0186) ===\nhsurj STAGES 1-2 LANDED in Picard/DivisorFamilyBackward.lean (green 8649 jobs, axiom-clean): (1) Scheme.LocalEquations.presentationDivisor_mul (LocalEquations-level divisor additivity along d.mul d', commit 87d787e49); (2) exists_localEquations_presentationDivisor_eq (every effective D is presentationDivisor of an explicit point-uniformizer-product LocalEquations, commit b2a85c0b6) \u2014 the eqns half of hsurj.\n\nCORRECTION to the \"hsurj needs NO general MV\" claim above: the support-separated backward construction is OBSTRUCTED for divisors with support in the chart overlap. The two pinned charts V0=pi^-1(chart0), V1=pi^-1(chart1) overlap (V0 inf V1 = pi^-1(Gm) nonempty affine), and a DivisorAdaptation structurally covers BOTH charts (FinCoverData.partition0/1 => cover0/cover1). So a support point z in V0 inf V1 is in a chart-0 AND a chart-1 piece; both equations vanish at z (coeffAt_eq_toAdd_ordZ_eqn), so the cross-chart ovlColength is NOT subsingleton and deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated's hsep is UNSATISFIABLE. This is the Cech H0 overlap correction (prod colength overcounts overlap points); the true finrank W needs the general MV = the hdeg wall. => general hsurj SHARES hdeg's MV obligation; only OFF-overlap divisors (supp subset (V0\\V1) union (V1\\V0)) are MV-free. DD-R's one-sided dictionary is MV-free only if P-fib's D avoids pi^-1(Gm). Full details + revised strategy in I-0186.",
