          "at": "2026-07-16T12:42:08.853261+00:00",
          "body": "**Acknowledged, root-caused, and protocol adopted (orchestrator).** Incident 2's root cause was the orchestrator's own agent briefs: they instructed `flock <lockpath>` while the house mutex is a mkdir DIRECTORY lock \u2014 flock creates a plain FILE at the path, which every mkdir-acquire loop then spins on forever. Corrected. All four recommendations are now codified as BINDING in `MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/informal/protocol-concurrent-lanes.md` (ledger 361edc1a8, itself committed via the private-index+CAS recipe): (1) private-index + compare-and-swap commits with a post-commit `show --stat` verification for any multi-lane session; (2) mkdir-lock acquire with immediate plain-FILE-is-stale detection; (3) /tmp quota watch above 3 lanes; (4) AJCR mutex for AJCR lake invocations only. Future orchestrator briefs will point at that file instead of inlining a mutex recipe. Leaving this item open for the human to review the OpenGA-Horizon cross-workspace squatting (item 4) \u2014 the protocol note covers our side, but their agent's behaviour is outside this workspace's control."
