      "body": "**T14 projectivity foundation \u2014 durable state + constraints (run 0014).** Four new files under `Picard/`; full build green (8606 jobs), DAG `0 dangling`.\n\n- `ProjectiveSpace.lean`: `\u2119(n;S)` = fibre product over `Spec \u2124` of `Proj \u2124[X\u1d62]`; `isProper_over`/`isSeparated_over`, `isPullback_map` \u2014 **axiom-clean**.\n- `SerreTwist.lean`: `serreTwist n m` = O(m) glued from `D\u208a(X\u1d62)` trivialisations, transitions `(X\u1d62/X\u2c7c)^m`. **One sorry `twistTransition_cocycle` (C2 triple-overlap transport)** taints everything mentioning `serreTwist` via `sorryAx`; rank-1 analogue of `bundleTransition_cocycle_transport`.\n- `ProjectiveMorphism.lean`: `Scheme.Hom.IsProjectiveWith \u03c0 L` (closed immersion into `\u2119(Fin(d+1);S)` with `L \u2245 i^*O(1)`, I-0118 encoding (a)); `isProper`/`comp_isClosedImmersion`/`baseChange` fully proved.\n- `SerreFiniteness.lean`: `sectionGradedModule_fg` **stated** under `IsProjectiveWith` (the deep Hilbert-lane leaf, `I-0109` item 1); genuine `sorry`.\n\nDurable constraints:\n- **Glue engine is universe-monomorphic** (`Scheme.Modules.glue` at `Scheme.GlueData.{0}`, `GlueDescent.lean:934`) \u21d2 `serreTwist`, the predicate and its stability facts live at `Scheme.{0}`; the `QuotScheme` restatement will specialise to `Scheme.{0}` unless the engine is generalised.\n- **`quot_boundedness` deliberately not stated in Lean**: a faithful Castelnuovo\u2013Mumford statement needs `R\u2071\u03c0_*`-of-twists vocabulary that does not exist; `lem:quot_boundedness` is a blueprint target (`\\lean` without `\\leanok`). Stating it loosely would repeat the `I-0118` trap.\n- O(1) sign convention: transition `i\u2192j` multiplies by `(X\u1d62/X\u2c7c)^m`; validate against `\u0393(\u2119\u207f, O(1)) =` linear forms once sections are computed.\n\nBlueprint: `sec:projective_vocabulary` (`Picard_QuotScheme.tex:5044`), 12 nodes, complete proofs, `\\source{nitsure-hilbert-quot}`.",
