      "body": "DD-4 field-vanishing feasibility: ARCHITECTURAL (bounded)\n\nVERDICT. The landed kappa(p)-base-fibre reduction chain is a DEAD END: it demands GLOBAL fibre divisibility (read psi in <read sec z> over the whole kappa(p)-fibre chart), which is FALSE by degree count. But the seed's sharp support condition is TRUE and reachable via a DIFFERENT single-point kappa(z) reduction the landed machinery does not deliver. Fix is bounded (~L), but a genuine pivot, not a patch of the current path.\n\nGAP (b) crux -- does the achiever cut d_p GLOBALLY? NO, only at z. read sec z is one section of the base-point-free, dim>=2 complete system divUniversalFibreKM = H0(N - d_p) (Fields:152-155; deg d_p = g, Fields:150). Its zero divisor E = (N - d_p) + div(read sec z) is effective of degree deg N - g >= 2 > 0. The achiever is a PER-POINT sInf witness (BaseDivisor:143-154, Nat.sInf_mem) pinning E only at z; at other points only the lower bound holds (BaseDivisor:128-139). Since dim T = deg N + 1 - 2g >= 2 (AssembleKappa:207-210), a closed argument (E<=B would force dim T = 1) shows read sec z MUST have a genuine extra zero w != z where a different reading (the achiever at w) has strictly smaller order, so read sec z does NOT divide it. <read sec z> strictly-inside the divisor ideal; global divisibility FAILS. This is exactly I-0288's wall, now closed by the degree identity.\n\nWHY the landed machinery cannot consume it: the 2c bridge (SeedFinish:115-156), germ lemma (RelDivisor:241-248) and flat lemma (RelDivisor:303-320) ALL comap/basePrime the point to the base prime p:Spec R and reduce to Subsingleton(N (x) kappa(p)) = readings dying over the WHOLE kappa(p)-fibre = the false global condition. The SHARP z not-in supp N z is iff-equivalent (mem_support_iff_nontrivial_residueField_tensorProduct applied at pz over Gamma(V); N z already Module.Finite Gamma(V) via chartColengthModule_finite, I-0303) to the SINGLE-POINT Subsingleton(N z (x)_Gamma(V) kappa(z)), which the achiever's single-point local generation at z CAN feed. The 2c bridge discarded the Gamma(V)-finiteness and re-derived a weaker R-finiteness purely to comap to R -- the fatal step.\n\nGAP (a) size: NON-mundane (needed flat is Flat R (Gamma(V)/(range + Gamma(V).read s)); the Gamma(V).read s term is a non-finite R-submodule, so the free-codomain keystone -- which needs a finite R source -- does not re-instantiate; quotient-of-flat is not flat). BUT MOOT: the flat lemma still consumes the same false global kappa(p) vanishing, so gap (a) sits downstream of the dead branch and never needs resolving on the current path.\n\nROUTE (recommended): (1) XS -- swap the reduction to mem_support_iff at pz over Gamma(V), target Subsingleton(N z (x) kappa(z)); (2) L -- the relative one-point stalk Nakayama I-0289 originally scoped but never built: base-change identification of N z's fibre at z with the kappa(p)-fibre colength at z (I-0302 2c's flagged isLocalization_stalk wiring) + achiever local-gen + a fibre->stalk flat lift (structural curve flat flat_sections_relPinnedChart, NOT the gap-(a) ideal-quotient flat). Single-point throughout, so the degree obstruction never fires. Plus (M) wire the achiever's uniform windowCompare != 0 into seedUniv.sec for hfib (residual wall 2). Reject the carve-direct non-seed alternative (I-0289 Q1b: 3 absent Gamma-local bridges, strictly harder, does not dodge this wall).\n\nNet: NOT finishable by pushing the current kappa(p) path (it ends in a false statement). Finishable by the bounded kappa(z) pivot (XS + L + M). The math is standard curve geometry (single-point local generation), not new theory.\n\nWorksheet informal/spec-dd4-fieldvanishing.md, commit 4963603d62871a1ed9061212dcb560c0162b2318.",
