ONE base-fibre vanishing Subsingleton(chartColengthModuleBase K b s \u2297_R \u03ba(p)) at p = comap(algebraMap R \u0393(V))(primeIdealOf z). Route is PURE mathlib finite-module support theory \u2014 NO isLocalization_stalk/germ detour: fibre-vanish \u27f9 p \u2209 supp_R N_R \u27f9 (Module.support_eq_zeroLocus, N_R finite over R) Ann_R(N_R) \u2284 p \u27f9 a killer r0 \u2208 Ann, r0 \u2209 p, so algebraMap r0 \u2209 primeIdealOf z (def of comap) annihilates every reading [read \u03c8] hence the whole \u0393(V)-span N z (Module.notMem_support_iff'). NB the landed DivSchemeRelDivisor germ machinery (link 2+3) is NOT needed for 2c \u2014 this annihilator route is shorter.\n\n=== RESIDUAL WALL 1 \u2014 RD-N field-vanishing (2b), XL, NOT closed ===\nThe bridge's hfib input Subsingleton(chartColengthModuleBase K b s \u2297 \u03ba(p)) is the honest wall. TWO genuine sub-gaps found by reading sources (both XL, ~multi-week per I-0289):\n (a) FLAT-TRANSPORT GAP: subsingleton_tmul_residueField_of_flat_quotient (RelDivisor:303) needs Module.Flat R ((\u0393(V)\u29f8\u27e8read s\u27e9)\u29f8N_RZ). This = \u0393(V)/(\u0393(V)\u00b7read s + range(chartReadMap)). The LANDED chart flat (flat_chart_colength_divUniversalSeedK, I-0302) is \u0393(V)/range(chartReadMap) \u2014 DIFFERS by \u0393(V)\u00b7read s vs R\u00b7read s (range is only the R-span). range(chartReadMap) is an R-submodule NOT a \u0393(V)-ideal, so the double-quotient does NOT collapse to the chart flat. The chart flat does NOT directly give the needed flat.\n (b) ACHIEVER FIBRE-DIVISIBILITY: field-vanishing = [read \u03c8] \u2297 1 = 0 for all \u03c8 \u2208 K = read \u03c8 \u2208 \u27e8read s\u27e9 over the WHOLE fibre chart \u03ba(p) (GLOBAL). The achiever (I-0291 exists_relThetaWindowEquiv_..._achieves_seedPrime, coeffAt=baseDivisorAt) gives achievement at a SINGLE fibre point z, NOT global divisibility. The OLD path (hfield_of_forall_pinnedPieceSectionsMap_mem, UnivFibreKerSpan:147) ALSO only REDUCED hfield to this same hdiv fibre-divisibility, never discharged it \u2014 so this is the genuine never-closed wall, unchanged by the redesign. Extra: the achiever is NOT yet wired into seedUniv.sec (current sec = exists_seedPoint OLD, DivSchemeSeedUnivGen:283), so even the single-point property is unavailable for the current sec.\n\n=== RESIDUAL WALL 2 \u2014 hfib, XL, NOT closed ===\nisGenerator_seedUniv' still needs hfib: under premise basicOpen(read(ann-cutter h z)) \u2260 \u22a5 at \u03ba(p), conclude read(sec z) \u2260 0. Reduces (via relPinnedSectionsMap_relThetaResSide_windowEquiv_ne_zero, Fields:251) to windowCompare R_Z \u03ba(p) x_z \u2260 0. The OLD seedUniv_hfib (Facts:300) got this from h z = algebraMap f + notMem_of_basicOpen_..._algebraMap_ne_bot \u27f9 f \u2209 p. For seedUniv' h z = ann-cutter (NOT algebraMap f) the premise does NOT give f \u2209 p; the OLD survival witness f (exists_seedPoint) does not connect to the ann-cutter neighbourhood. Needs either the achiever wired into sec z (uniform fibre nonvanishing) or a new D(ann-cutter)-nonempty \u27f9 f\u2209p argument. BLOCKED same as wall 1's achiever-wiring.\n\n=== NEXT (for the follow-up lane) ===\n1. Wire the I-0291 achiever into seedUniv.sec (replace exists_seedPoint), giving windowCompare uniform \u27f9 discharges hfib (wall 2) directly.\n2. Close wall 1: needs (a) the RIGHT flat Module.Flat R ((\u0393(V)\u29f8\u27e8read s\u27e9)\u29f8N_RZ) (NOT the chart flat) AND (b) achiever single-point \u27f9 global fibre divisibility (the genuine XL, the P-fib d_p content). Then feed my bridge notMem_support_chartColengthModule_of_subsingleton_tmul_residueField to get SeedUnivRDN, \u27f9 unconditional isGenerator_seedUniv' \u27f9 certificate \u27f9 U1=divUniversalFamily=divFamEps_certifiedFamily (DDR9-U). Certificate (DivSchemeCertificateEngine) + U1 (DivSchemeEps:312) NOT reached this lane (blocked on unconditional isGenerator).",
