      "body": "redesign seedUniv revision + fibre-cutter BUILD \u2014 the ann-based fibre-cutter ENGINE + the redesigned seed's DIRECT isGenerator landed (all keystones green, axiom-clean, committed). The concrete seedUniv' value + RD-N pinned (blocked on brick-1 carve wiring hsub_seedUniv, I-0290).\n\n=== COMMITS (this lane) ===\n- 1682735d8  DD-4 redesign: the ann-based fibre-cutter engine (h z in ann(N z)) + DIRECT hdvd. New file Picard/DivSchemeRedesignFibreCut.lean (160 L).\n- e82a876cd  DD-4 redesign: the redesigned seed's isGenerator from the ann-cutter. New file Picard/DivSchemeRedesignSeed.lean (83 L).\nBoth single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake build GREEN under the mkdir lock (7.4s / 6.6s, 8661/8665 jobs). Root: HEAD-blob + only my import lines (after DivSchemeRedesignAchiever, then DivSchemeRedesignFibreCut); sibling working-tree PicEtCrossBaseGraph add + Hinj/Achiever removals NOT swept. Zero sorries, zero new warnings (Pic.lean show + Challenge.lean sorries pre-existing).\n\n=== THE FIBRE-CUTTER: I-0288 fact 2 DISSOLVED (h z NO LONGER algebraMap f) ===\nThe old h z = algebraMap f (base-only) made D(h z) the WHOLE fibre chart (I-0288), so hle demanded achievement everywhere. The redesign's h z in ann(N z) is a GENUINE relative fibre-cutter: on D(h z) the base ideal J z collapses to <read sec z>, so hdvd is DIRECT. Probe (I-0289 \u00a72) confirmed NO in-tree relative fibre-cutter existed; ann(N z) via mathlib Module.support is the route, built here.\n\n=== KEYSTONES (VERBATIM; namespace AlgebraicGeometry, R = abstract test ring) ===\n\n(1) exists_mem_annihilator_notMem_of_notMem_support {A} [CommRing A] (N) [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module.Finite A N] {p : PrimeSpectrum A} (hp : p not-in Module.support A N) : exists h : A, h in Module.annihilator A N and h not-in p.asIdeal\n  \u2014 the pure CA core (Module.mem_support_iff_of_finite + SetLike.not_le_iff_exists).\n\n(2) IsAffineOpen.exists_mem_basicOpen_forall_smul_eq_zero {X : Scheme} {V : X.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (N) [AddCommGroup N] [Module Gamma(X,V) N] [Module.Finite Gamma(X,V) N] {z : X} (hz : z in V) (hsupp : hV.primeIdealOf <z,hz> not-in Module.support Gamma(X,V) N) : exists h : Gamma(X,V), z in X.basicOpen h and forall n : N, h . n = 0\n  \u2014 the fibre-cutter EXISTENCE: z not-in supp(N z) (= RD-N) gives the ann cutter h with z in D(h). Point->prime via IsAffineOpen.primeIdealOf / fromSpec_primeIdealOf / fromSpec_preimage_basicOpen.\n\n(3) Scheme.resHom_mem_span_singleton_of_mul_mem {X : Scheme} {U : X.Opens} (h e s : Gamma(X,U)) (hmul : h*s in Ideal.span {e}) : X.resHom (X.basicOpen_le h) s in Ideal.span {X.resHom (X.basicOpen_le h) e}\n  \u2014 the DIRECT-hdvd engine: h unit on D(h) (Scheme.isUnit_resHom_of_eq_basicOpen) => the cofactor divides through.\n\n(4) ThetaGeneratorSeed.hdvd_of_forall_smul_relThetaResSide_mem_span (D) (hann : forall z {psi}, psi in K -> D.h z * relThetaResSide a (D.side z) le_rfl psi in Ideal.span {relThetaResSide a (D.side z) le_rfl (D.sec z)}) : forall z {psi}, psi in K -> relThetaResSide a (D.side z) (D.piece_le z) psi in Ideal.span {D.eqn z}\n  \u2014 the seed-shaped DIRECT hdvd: the ann containment per point IS the hdvd clause of isGenerator_of_fibre_ne_zero, via resHom_relThetaResSide.\n\n(5) ThetaGeneratorSeed.isGenerator_of_ann_cutter (D) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 C.hom] [GeometricallyIrreducible C.hom] (hann : the (4) ann containment) (hfib : achiever fibrewise nonvanishing, the isGenerator_of_fibre_ne_zero shape) : D.IsGenerator\n  = D.isGenerator_of_fibre_ne_zero (D.hdvd_of_forall_smul_relThetaResSide_mem_span hann) hfib\n  \u2014 the redesigned isGenerator_seedUniv: SIMPLER finale (DivSchemeSeed:188), NOT the fibrewise-ker-span capstone; DIRECT hdvd, no per-fibre hfield.\n\n=== RESIDUAL \u2014 the concrete seedUniv' + RD-N (next lane) ===\n1. seedUniv' VALUE: mirror the old seedUniv (DivSchemeSeedUnivGen.lean Classical.choose per point), swap sec := exists_relThetaWindowEquiv_mem_divUniversalSeedK_achieves_seedPrime (brick 2, I-0291), h := the ann-cutter (2). The h field needs, per z, the premise 'z not-in supp(N z)' over Gamma(chart) \u2014 i.e. RD-N. seedUniv'.IsGenerator is then isGenerator_of_ann_cutter (hann from the ann-cutter's smul_eq_zero -> mul-in-span, hfib from the achiever windowCompare!=0 span bridge, exactly as old seedUniv's hfib).\n2. RD-N (read_sec_generates_stalk, spec \u00a71.3): span{read sec z} = J z at stalk O_z, equivalently hV.primeIdealOf z not-in Module.support Gamma(chart) (N z). Inputs: (i) read sec z in J z; (ii) achiever generates J-bar_p at z (brick 2); (iii) J z R_Z-flat (brick 1, forall_flat_colength_quotient_of_hspan, I-0290, but its hsub_seedUniv carve wiring is the UNBUILT XL residual). Proof shape: flat => J cap pGamma = pJ (no Tor_1), J-bar_p = J/pJ, Nakayama over O_z. The k[eps] guard (I-0231) lives here: MUST route through flatness. To feed the fibre-cutter (2), bridge Module.support Gamma(chart) at primeIdealOf z to the stalk O_z via hV.isLocalization_stalk.\n3. hann from smul: the cutter (2) gives 'forall n : N z, h . n = 0' with N z = image of readings mod <read sec z>; that yields 'h z * read psi in <read sec z>' (hann shape of (4)/(5)) once N z is set up as the chart-level sideColengthSubmodule analog (over the chart V, le_rfl, not the piece).",
