      "body": "DD-4 redesign feasibility: HARD-BUT-BUILDABLE (sound, unblockable, ~2 XL + 3 L + 2 M bricks, multi-week; NO impossibility). Worksheet informal/spec-dd4-redesign.md, commit 6e35e7ea3d48d9361353d0ed6fcbaf15e0cb236d.\n\n=== THE DECISIVE ANSWER (task Q1b: does a carve-direct NON-seed relDivisor dissolve the achiever-lift?) ===\nThe achiever-lift (I-0258) dissolves EITHER WAY, so skipping the seed buys nothing and costs more. KEEP THE SEED; redesign (sec z, h z). A fully carve-direct non-seed CertifiedDivisorFamily (build base ideal J as a Module.Invertible line bundle over Gamma(relCurve), read off LocalEquations.eqn) IS possible but strictly HARDER: it needs THREE bridges ABSENT in mathlib+in-tree \u2014 (i) R-flat + fibrewise-invertible => invertible, (ii) rank-1 projective => Module.Invertible (mathlib has NO converse), (iii) invertible ideal => single local generator J.Gamma_f = span{eqn}. All three are Gamma-LOCAL (curve-local), whereas every landed engine (SlicingFlatKernel, SupportTubeFinite, the carve) is R_Z-FIBREWISE. The seed route reaches the SAME local generator via R_Z-fibrewise flatness + a one-point stalk Nakayama, reusing maximal landed surface.\n\n=== WHY THE ACHIEVER-LIFT IS NOT ACTUALLY A WALL (dissolves I-0258/I-0288 (A)) ===\nsec z = a relative achiever AT z, built by lifting a kappa(p)-fibre achiever THROUGH the SURJECTION read (x) kappa(p) : K_univ (x) kappa(p) ->> H0(N - d_p) (divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span, DivSchemeSeedUnivRes:376) + exists_coeffAt_eq_baseDivisorAt (BaseDivisor:143). I-0258 is TRUE (a single window vector need not reduce to a CHOSEN f_p) but IRRELEVANT: we need SOME achiever, and the surjection hits every element of the window. A clean lift, not the non-liftable step the history feared.\n\n=== THE FIBRE-CUTTER (dissolves I-0288 (B)) ===\nh z is NOT algebraMap f (base-only; makes D(h) the WHOLE fibre chart, exactly why I-0288 hle failed). Instead h z in ann(N z), N z := J/(read sec z) finite over R_Z (SupportTubeFinite, I-0244), at z not in supp(N z). ann(N z) elements are GENUINE fibre-cutters. NOTE: probe found NO fibre-cutter over general R exists in-tree \u2014 only PointDivisor over a FIELD base (PointDivisor:190/278); ann(N z) is the in-tree route to a relative cutter.\n\n=== THE ONE GENUINE WALL + SIZES ===\nRD-N (relative-local-BPF stalk Nakayama, size L): read(sec z) generates J at stalk O_z from fibre generation + J R_Z-FLAT. Flatness load-bearing (J cap pGamma = pJ, no Tor_1) \u2014 WITHOUT it the k[eps] trap (I-0231) fires. Then hdvd on D(h z) is DIRECT (feed simpler isGenerator_of_fibre_ne_zero, DivSchemeSeed:188, NOT the fibrewise-ker-span capstone). Prerequisite (size XL, largest lane): J R_Z-flat via SlicingFlatKernel c4 (:296) on the reading map read, fed by divUniversal_carve_residueField (FamilyUniv:135) \u2014 I-0284 hspan content, cleaner (no chosen eqn z). Then no-leak from proper support (I-0285 reduction), certificate non-circular (dvd holds), divUniversalFamily := divFamEps_certifiedFamily (DivSchemeEps:312) = DDR9-U U1.\n\nFile plan (anti-circular, dvd BEFORE certificate): (1) J-flat XL -> (2) achiever M -> (3) RD-N/hdvd L -> (4) seed/isGenerator M -> (5) no-leak L -> (6) certificate L -> (7) U1 L.\n\nFallback if (1)/(3) wall: the fully carve-direct non-seed family (needs the 3 absent Gamma-local bridges) or Sym^g/Hilbert plan-B. Supersedes I-0268 spec-dd4-seam.md whose relDivisor routed through seedUniv.localEquations (I-0272).",
