      "body": "DD-R SPEC LANDED (informal/spec-dd-r.md, commit 8c12b88cb) \u2014 the two gate ADJUDICATIONS decided, evidence file:line in the spec.\n\nVERDICT A (I-0186 item 2 x I-0182): the off-overlap normalization is mathematically UNAVAILABLE \u2014 P-fib's divisor is the modulus itself (existsUnique_effective_divisor_of_carve, RiemannRoch/PFib.lean:241, D := baseDivisor of the GIVEN window, :282, pinned pointwise by baseDivisorAt_normalization :127); as the Z(diamond)-point varies D ranges over ALL effective deg-g divisors including g*x for x in pi^-1(Gm); no translation/rescale exists. BUT DD-R consumes NEITHER hsurj NOR hdeg: the recover direction is pullback of a UNIVERSAL certified family built by local generators from the universal carve pair (worksheet 3.4.1) \u2014 divFamOfDivisor appears nowhere; the only degree identity needed is fibrewise FOR CARVE-CERTIFIED FAMILIES and closes MV-free by the certified-degree pinch (corank g [DD-4 Task 5] + SectionBound:248 => deg <= 2g + exact rank_normalization WindowLedger:396 => deg = g). I-0182's one-sided-dictionary route is SUPERSEDED for DD-R. The hsurj/overlap obstruction MIGRATES TO DAT-B's coverage row (binding boundary flag in spec 1); designed relief recorded: DD-R's field instance gives a window-route divFamOfDivisor for ALL D (certificate from the second window, no support separation) \u2014 I-0186 stages 3-5 potentially moot for DAT-B. hdeg stays the sole XL, UNFUNDED and UNCONSUMED. Fallback if DDR-4/DDR-8 wall: matrix-chart AMBER (worksheet 3.6(d)), NOT general MV (it would not unblock the relative bricks).\n\nVERDICT B (I-0159 trailing (ii)): CHART-LOCAL SUFFICES \u2014 glued grPoint : (T -> grOver) -> grFunctor value is NOT consumed by DD-R, stays deferred. Family->hom is the GRQ grPointOfRankQuotient pattern (GrassmannianQuot.lean:4984, functor-value->scheme-map gluing) on the LANDED chart kit: matrixPoint_factors_chart_iff (GrassmannianChartFrame.lean:271), chartTautologicalPoint (GrassmannianTa