      "body": "DD-1c (f) hsurj lane \u2014 STAGES 1-2 LANDED + a BLOCKING OBSTRUCTION for stages 3-5 (2026-07-17, Opus hsurj prover). Follow-on to I-0182/I-0179/I-0171/I-0167. New file Picard/DivisorFamilyBackward.lean (root-wired, green 8649 jobs, keystones lean_verify axiom-clean [propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound]).\n\nLANDED (two committed green stages, the \"eqns\" half of hsurj):\n- Stage 1 (commit 87d787e49): Scheme.LocalEquations.mul_presentation_elem + Scheme.LocalEquations.presentationDivisor_mul. The Weil divisor of the pointwise product d.mul d' is the SUM: presentationDivisor K (d.mul d').presentation = presentationDivisor K d.presentation + presentationDivisor K d'.presentation. Proof: the product presentation's trivializing elem is the product of elems (germ_res_apply + map_mul), and ordZ is a group hom so orders/coeffs add. LocalEquations-level companion of the landed MeromorphicPresentation.presentationDivisor_mul.\n- Stage 2 (commit b2a85c0b6): Scheme.LocalEquations.unitEquations (trivial system, presentationDivisor = 0) + Scheme.LocalEquations.exists_localEquations_presentationDivisor_eq: every EFFECTIVE divisor D (0<=D) is presentationDivisor K E.presentation for an explicit LocalEquations E (a mul-product of tracked point-uniformizer pointEquations, one factor per unit of multiplicity, via stage-1 additivity + presentationDivisor_pointEquations; Finsupp.induction over the support with effectivity propagated). LocalEquations-level companion of exists_presentationDivisor_eq (which only gives a MeromorphicPresentation); effectivity is what keeps it regular (no inverse/pole factors). This gives the anchor equations F.eqns of a family realizing D.\n\nTHE OBSTRUCTION (why stages 3-5 \u2014 the certified support-separated adaptation + divFamOfDivisor \u2014 are NOT MV-free for general D, correcting I-0182/I-0179): The two pinned charts of relCurve are V0 = pi^-1(P1 chart0), V1 = pi^-1(P1 chart1); they OVERLAP, V0 inf V1 = pi^-1(Gm) is a nonempty affine open (AffineTwoCover.pullbackProd; P1 charts overlap on Gm). A DivisorAdaptation structurally covers BOTH charts: FinCoverData.partition0/1 (sum a_j h_j = 1) force V0 <= sup(chart-0 pieces) and V1 <= sup(chart-1 pieces) (FinCoverData.cover0/cover1). So any closed point z in V0 inf V1 lies in some chart-0 piece (inl a) AND some chart-1 piece (inr b). If z in supp(D), then BOTH piece equations vanish at z to order coeffAt_z(D) != 0 \u2014 every adaptation equation refines d and reads D's coefficient at every point of its piece (DivisorAdaptation.coeffAt_eq_toAdd_ordZ_eqn) \u2014 so neither is a unit at z and the overlap ideal (eqn_inl_a, eqn_inr_b) is contained in the maximal ideal m_z != top. Hence ovlColength (inl a)(inr b) is NOT subsingleton, and the support-separation hypothesis hsep of deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated / subsingleton_ovlColength_of_sep is UNSATISFIABLE for any D whose support meets V0 inf V1.\n\nMathematically this is exactly the Cech H0 overlap correction: for z in the overlap, prod_j colength OVERCOUNTS z's local degree (once per chart), so the separated formula finrank W = sum colength gives the WRONG (too-large) degree; the true finrank W = sum colength - overlap correction = the general Mayer-Vietoris (= the hdeg wall). CONCLUSION: hsurj for a GENERAL effective deg-n divisor is NOT free of the general-MV wall \u2014 it needs it precisely for overlap-support divisors, sharing hdeg's obligation. The support-separated backward construction only realizes divisors supported OFF the overlap: supp(D) subset (V0 minus V1) union (V1 minus V0); those DO round-trip MV-free (the off-chart pieces have unit equations, cross-chart overlaps are trivially separated, and within one affine chart finitely many support points can be isolated by basic opens).\n\nREVISED STRATEGY / what remains:\n1. The MV-free hsurj is achievable ONLY for off-overlap divisors. To close it needs: (a) the point-separation-within-one-affine-chart infrastructure (given finitely many closed pts in an affine, a basic-open refinement of d.cover isolating each in a unique piece with the others' pieces avoiding them) \u2014 NEW infra, medium; plus (b) finite-colength + the field-trivial certificate (c3/c4 free, rank via deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated). Stages 1-2 already supply the eqns.\n2. For DD-R's one-sided dictionary (I-0182): still MV-free IFF P-fib's unique effective deg-n divisor D can be arranged/normalized to be supported OFF the chart overlap. If P-fib's D always avoids pi^-1(Gm) (e.g. supported at a fixed rational point at infinity), hsurj-for-D + divFamDivisor_injective (landed) closes it MV-free. Otherwise the field dictionary genuinely needs the general-MV wall for BOTH directions \u2014 recommend the human/DD-R spec confirm P-fib's support location.\n3. The general (all-D) field dictionary equiv divFamFieldEquivOfDegOfSurj needs the general MV (hdeg) regardless \u2014 it is now the sole XL for BOTH hdeg and general hsurj.\n\nagent-ready",
