      "body": "DD-1c (f) THE WALL (I-0171) FALLS for the support-separated case (2026-07-17, Opus prover). Follow-on to I-0171/I-0167 (both KEPT OPEN as machinery maps for the remaining stages).\n\nLANDED: Picard/DivisorFamilyFieldDegree.lean (NEW, root-wired, green 8863 jobs, keystones lean_verify axiom-clean [propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound]). Commits 4861d8a27 (stage1 MV additivity), 526dd6ff2 (stage2a dictionary+per-piece coeff), 25536cd39 (stage2b per-piece finrank), 14c2dca9d (stage3 assembly + deg=n), fb62d9144 (root wire).\n\nThe colength<->degree identity I-0171 flagged as THE WALL, closed for the support-separated case (each piece equation f_i a unit on every overlap):\n- DivisorAdaptation.deg_presentationDivisor_eq_finrank_glued: deg K (presentationDivisor d) = finrank K W(d).\n- deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated: deg K (divFamDivisor (mk F)) = n (adds the field half IsCertified.finrank_glued). THIS unlocks step (iv): backward-map adaptations are support-separated by construction (pointEquations products isolate support points).\n\nREUSABLE CORES (public): Scheme.isUnit_germ_iff_ordZ_eq_one (unit germ <-> trivial order, via DVR valuation_eq_one_iff_notMem -- packages the PRIVATE ChartColength lemmas); DivisorAdaptation.coeffAt_eq_toAdd_ordZ_eqn (order of any piece eqn = coeffAt divisor, via ordZ_germGenericUnits + ordZ_elem_eq); finrank_glued_eq_sum_of_separated (equalizer = product Pi_j colength when overlaps subsingleton, finrank_pi_fintype); finrank_colength_eq_sum (per-piece finrank = local degree via finrank_quotient_span_section, empty pieces=0); coeffAt_eq_zero_of_isUnit_germ; subsingleton_ovlColength_of_sep (overlap ideal = top via isUnit_of_isUnit_germ). Separation hypothesis 'each f_i a unit on overlaps' both implies Subsingleton(ovlColength) AND gives support-point uniqueness (avoids prime/affine-overlap machinery).\n\nSTILL OPEN (the (f) endgame): (1) GENERAL forward case deg K (divFamDivisor F) = n for an ARBITRARY certified adaptation -- needs honest Mayer-Vietoris overlap inclusion-exclusion. NOTE (checked this session): the refine-to-separated shortcut does NOT close it -- deg D = finrank W(A') for a constructed separated A' is circular (deg D = deg D); getting = n still needs deg D = finrank W(A) for the ORIGINAL arbitrary A, i.e. genuine general MV. This is the remaining XL. (2) backward map (iv): build a support-separated CertifiedDivisorFamily from an effective divisor via PointPresentation.pointEquations products; its degree check is now deg_divFamDivisor_of_separated. (3) inverse laws (v) + assembling divFamFieldEquiv (RefinementInjectivity). divFamFieldEquiv NOT yet assembled.",
