      "body": "agent-ready\n\nhinj_seedUniv (hspan core) BUILD \u2014 hinj REDUCED to the cleanest carve target (fibre non-collapse of N z); hinj_seedUniv itself NOT landed (the carve rank-g wall is unchanged, needs the UNBUILT section\u2192functionField germ bridge).\n\nNew file Picard/DivSchemeUnivFibreHinj.lean (137 L, \u2264500). Single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake build GREEN under the mkdir lock (8671 jobs, 37s); both keystones lean_verify axioms exactly [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; zero sorries; zero new warnings. Full-root stays GREEN.\n\n=== COMMITS (this lane, namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaGeneratorSeed; section vars {k C R \u03c0 a K} (D : ThetaGeneratorSeed C R \u03c0 a K)) ===\n- 368351068  hspan \u27f9 hinj converse (completes hinj \u27fa hspan)\n- 6e73431d5  hinj reduced to fibre-injectivity of N z \u21aa colength z (the carve target)\n\n=== KEYSTONES (VERBATIM) ===\n(1) liftQ_rTensor_injective_of_ker_rTensor_le (D)\n    (hspan : \u2200 (z : relCurve C R)(p : PrimeSpectrum R), LinearMap.ker (((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype).rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField) \u2264 LinearMap.range ((LinearMap.ker ((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype)).subtype.rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField))\n    : \u2200 (z)(p : PrimeSpectrum R), Function.Injective (((LinearMap.ker ((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype)).liftQ ((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype) le_rfl).rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField)\n  \u2014 the CONVERSE of hspan_of_forall_liftQ_rTensor_injective (KerSpan:190). Together they give hinj \u27fa hspan. Proof: f_z\u2297\u03ba = (f\u0304_z\u2297\u03ba)\u2218(mkQ\u2297\u03ba), mkQ\u2297\u03ba surjective, rTensor_exact on ker f_z \u21aa K \u21a0 K\u29f8ker f_z.\n(2) hinj_of_forall_sideColengthSubmodule_subtype_rTensor_injective (D)\n    (hsub : \u2200 (z)(p : PrimeSpectrum R), Function.Injective ((D.sideColengthSubmodule z).subtype.rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField))\n    : \u2200 (z)(p : PrimeSpectrum R), Function.Injective (((LinearMap.ker ((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype)).liftQ ((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype) le_rfl).rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField)\n  \u2014 hinj FROM fibre-injectivity of the K-side-component submodule inclusion N z = sideColengthSubmodule z (= range f_z). Proof: range f\u0304_z = N z, so f\u0304_z corestricts to an equiv \u0113 : K\u29f8ker f_z \u2243\u2097 N z; f\u0304_z\u2297\u03ba = (N z.subtype\u2297\u03ba)\u2218(\u0113\u2297\u03ba) = (fibre-injective inclusion)\u2218(equiv) injective.\n\n=== THE REDUCTION CHAIN NOW ===\nInjective((seedUniv\u2026).sideColengthSubmodule z).subtype.rTensor \u03ba(p))  [hsub_seedUniv]\n  \u2192(2)\u2192 hinj_seedUniv  \u2192(hspan_of_forall_liftQ_rTensor_injective, KerSpan:190)\u2192 hspan_seedUniv\n  \u2192(isGenerator_of_fibrewise_ker_span_of_field_vanishing, Close:84)\u2192 IsGenerator.\nSo the SEED CLOSE now needs ONLY hsub_seedUniv (+ hfield + the 4 cheap facts). hsub is the cleanest possible carve statement: N z \u21aa colength z stays injective in every residue fibre (no fibre collapse) = the carve rank-g pinning. NOTE it is ALSO exactly the flat-quotient fact (flat(colength/N) \u27f9 hsub \u27f9 hspan), so dvd_of_flat_quotient_of_field_vanishing (SeedDvd:128, takes hflat directly) is the equivalent route; either hsub OR hflat = Module.Flat R_Z (colength z \u29f8 sideColengthSubmodule z) closes the seed.\n\n=== RESIDUAL \u2014 hsub_seedUniv (the genuine carve rank-g wall, UNCHANGED difficulty, XL) ===\nNeed: at seedUniv (R = R_Z = DivCarveChartRing, K = divUniversalSeedK), Function.Injective ((sideColengthSubmodule z).subtype.rTensor \u03ba(p)) for all z,p. This is N z \u2297 \u03ba(p) \u21aa colength z \u2297 \u03ba(p) injective \u2014 the carve rank pinning that the induced fibre kernel is trivial. Route (I-0284): pinnedPieceQuotBaseChangeAlg (KerSpan, colength\u2297\u03ba \u2245 fibre colength) + the fibre window identification divUniversalFibreKM (AssembleKappa:157; corank g via finrank_divUniversalFibreKM_add:207) + divUniversal_carve_residueField (FamilyUniv:135, carvePairArrow=0) + ker_baseChange_mkQ (DivCarveKit:91) + divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span (Res:376). BLOCKER = the still-UNBUILT section\u2192functionField germ bridge (relThetaResSide on D(h') \u2194 thetaFieldRead) flagged in I-0284 as the first sub-brick \u2014 it identifies the piece colength fibre with the fibre-window reading, needed to see N z\u2297\u03ba inside the carve cokernel. Until that brick lands, hsub_seedUniv cannot be wired to the carve rank data. No FibreInjective (I-0279/I-0281 dead). No sorries; full-root GREEN.",
