      "body": "hcolFin closed-trace BUILD \u2014 REDUCTION landed (engine + all instances discharged), single topological residual. New file Picard/DivSchemeSeedUnivColFin.lean (247 L), single-module lake build GREEN (52s, LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1), 3 keystones lean_verify axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], zero sorries, warning-free. Root: HEAD-blob + own line only (sibling PicEtCrossBaseGraph line NOT swept).\n\n=== COMMITS (this lane) ===\n- 4ec2a0d60  closed-trace reduction infra: topology + abstract-engine wrapper + generic seed reduction\n- 819f9dbc2  seedUniv_hcolFin_of_forall_closure_subset (hcolFin at seedUniv reduced to the no-leak)\n\n=== KEYSTONES (namespace AlgebraicGeometry) ===\n- isClosed_sdiff_basicOpen_of_closure_subset {X}{V:X.Opens}(g:\u0393(X,V)) (hcl : closure ((V:Set)\\(X.basicOpen g:Set)) \u2286 (V:Set)) : IsClosed ((V:Set)\\(X.basicOpen g:Set))  \u2014 plus _of_forall_fibre (\u03c6:X\u27f6S) fibrewise spelling. The other inclusion closure \u2286 (D g)\u1d9c is automatic.\n- IsAffineOpen.finite_quotient_span_singleton_of_closure_subset : the abstract engine (SupportTubeFinite:215) in closure-subset spelling. ANTI-CIRCULAR: uses no DivisorAdaptation.\n- ThetaGeneratorSeed.hcolFin_of_forall_closure_subset / _of_forall_fibre (D)(hnoleak) : \u2200 z, Module.Finite R (\u0393(relCurve C R, D.piece z) \u29f8 Ideal.span {D.eqn z})  \u2014 the exact hcolFin hypothesis shape of isGenerator_of_fibrewise_ker_span_of_field_vanishing, for ANY seed, from the pure topological no-leak. (needs [UniversallyClosed]+[LocallyOfFiniteType] on relCurve C R \u2198 Spec R.)\n- seedUniv_hcolFin_of_forall_closure_subset (VERBATIM the assembly feed) : (hnoleak : \u2200 z, closure ((seedUniv\u2026).piece z \\ D((seedUniv\u2026).eqn z)) \u2286 (seedUniv\u2026).piece z) \u2192 \u2200 z, Module.Finite R_Z (\u0393(relCurve C R_Z,(seedUniv\u2026).piece z) \u29f8 Ideal.span {(seedUniv\u2026).eqn z}).  ALL instance plumbing discharged (UniversallyClosed+LocallyOfFiniteType fire from instIsProperRelCurveHom under [IsProper C.hom]).\n\n=== hcolFin STATUS: reduced, NOT yet landed ===\nhcolFin at seedUniv = seedUniv_hcolFin_of_forall_closure_subset applied to the SINGLE residual\n  hnoleak_seedUniv : \u2200 z, closure ((seedUniv\u2026).piece z \\ D(eqn z)) \u2286 (seedUniv\u2026).piece z\n(equivalently the fibrewise no-leak \u2200 z s, \u03c6\u207b\u00b9{s} \u2229 closure(piece z \\ D(eqn z)) \u2286 piece z, via _of_forall_fibre). piece z \\ D(eqn z) = piece z \u2229 V(sec z) (V(sec z) = the seed section's zero-locus, closed); the trace is closed iff its closure stays in the piece.\n\n=== FINDING (the no-leak is genuine geometry, NOT free) ===\nThe no-leak's discharge needs the seed section's relative divisor V(eqn z) to be PROPER over the WHOLE base R_Z and CONTAINED in the piece (a dominant-piece / fibrewise-no-leak containment).  Fibrewise-NONVANISHING (all the f-choice exists_forall_windowCompare_ne_zero gives: windowCompare \u2260 0 on D(f), piece z = chart \u2229 \u03c6\u207b\u00b9(D(f))) is INSUFFICIENT.  Toy counterexample confirming the subtlety: trivial P\u00b9 family over R=k[t], section cutting {x=t}, piece over D(t) \u2014 colength k[t,1/t] is NOT R-finite and the trace leaks to the base point (t=0,x=0)\u2209piece.  So hcolFin genuinely requires the seed design's containment (I-0280's 'D(h z) contains the whole fibre branch of d_p'), which is currently only PROSE \u2014 no landed Lean lemma expresses V(eqn z) \u2286 piece z or the fibrewise no-leak.  NEXT LANE: prove hnoleak_seedUniv (best route: establish V(eqn z) \u2286 piece z as a closed containment from the seed's h z / d_p design, then closure is trivial) and feed seedUniv_hcolFin_of_forall_closure_subset.  No DivisorAdaptation (anti-circular).\n\nAssembly unchanged: isGenerator_of_fibrewise_ker_span_of_field_vanishing D hreg hcolFin hcolFlat hspan hfield hfib \u2014 hreg/hcolFlat/hfib landed (I-0283); hspan/hfield sibling; hcolFin = seedUniv_hcolFin_of_forall_closure_subset \u2218 hnoleak_seedUniv (residual).",
