      "body": "DAT-B B-5 partial \u2014 the SHARED plus-class collapse lemma LANDED; coverage core (COV-1) blocked at the C9/divRep boundary.\n\nFILE: MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/PicEtAffFieldCollapse.lean (111 L). Commit c295fb0c3 (private-index CAS; root = HEAD blob + only my line, protocol s4 \u2014 sibling PicEtCrossBaseGraph line NOT swept). Zero sorries; both keystones axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake green under mkdir lock (8629 jobs); zero warnings in my file.\n\nSHARED PLUS-CLASS COLLAPSE LEMMA (the name B-4 consumes) \u2014 KEYSTONE 1 (verbatim):\ntheorem PicEtAff.map_mk_eq_unit_of_algHom {K L : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra k K] [Field L] [Algebra k L] [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower k K L] {E : Algebra.EtaleCover K} (x : descentClasses C E) (l : E.Carrier -a[K] L) : PicEtAff.map C L (PicEtAff.mk C E x) = PicEtAff.unit C L (relPicAlgMap C (l.restrictScalars k) (x : relPic C (overSpec k E.Carrier)))\nContext: {k}[Field k](C : Over (Spec (.of k))) ONLY \u2014 NO hypotheses on C.hom (pure plus construction). Proof: map_mk reads the L-restriction as mk(E.baseChange L)(descentBaseChange x); unit_eq_mk reads the target unit on the same cover; the descent/cocycle condition relPicAlgMap_congr (baseChangeInclude vs ofId comp l, through descentBaseChange_coe) identifies the two descent classes. The honest class is relPicAlgMap l x, EXACTLY the degAff_mk honest class (DegreeZero.lean:273).\n\nKEYSTONE 2 (verbatim, Cech form the degree seam + exists_cechPicClass_eq consume):\ntheorem PicEtAff.map_mk_eq_unit_relPicMk_of_algHom {K L : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra k K] [Field L] [Algebra k L] [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower k K L] {E : Algebra.EtaleCover K} (x : descentClasses C E) (l : E.Carrier -a[K] L) : exists M : (C (X) overSpec k L).left.CechPic, PicEtAff.map C L (PicEtAff.mk C E x) = PicEtAff.unit C L (relPicMk C (overSpec k L) M)\nProof: relPicMk_surjective on the honest class + keystone 1.\n\nHOW B-4 / B-5 CONSUME IT: write the fibre plus class as mk E x (PicEtAff.ind / picEtAffineEquiv); field cofinality Algebra.EtaleCover.exists_finiteSeparableField_algHom (EtaleCover.lean:287) gives L finite separable + l : E.Carrier -a[K] L; apply keystone 1/2. The L/K/k tower is a CLEAN instance hypothesis (campaign-idiomatic, cf DivSchemeSeed.lean:73). Well-definedness across splittings = E-iv-alg + ClassCohomology:111 (not re-derived here).\n\nNEW WALL / GOTCHA (verified this pass, MEMORY-WORTHY for B-4/B-5/B-6): the I-0236 two-level-tower diamond is a GENUINE whnf NON-TERMINATION (not merely slow \u2014 still times out at 1,000,000 heartbeats). Instantiating L with a RingHom.toAlgebra composite letI (letI : Algebra k L := ((algebraMap K L).comp (algebraMap k K)).toAlgebra, the DegreeZero.lean:339 pattern) EXPLODES the moment PicEtAff.map C L unfolds the base-changed etale carrier (a MvPolynomial-quotient). This is why the collapse is stated with the tower as CLEAN hypotheses and NOT bundled as an existential over-instances of a cofinality-produced L. degAff_mul survives the same composite letI only because degAff never forms map/baseChange. CONSEQUENCE: B-5 coverage step 1 and B-4 link-2 (etale-carrier image transport) MUST supply the fibre extension L via a NATIVE k-algebra tower (residue-field-based instances), never a composite letI, or they hit this wall. respectTransparency false + maxSynthPendingDepth 3 do NOT fix it.\n\nC9 / divRep BOUNDARY (where B-5 stops, per worksheet): chartLocus is still UNDEFINED (DAT-C C9 unshipped, confirmed I-0252). Therefore COV-1 pic0_chartLocus_cover CANNOT YET BE STATED. Its target predicate is the witness/h1=0 form of Pic0ChartLocusOpen keystone isOpen_setOf_exists_witness_h1_vanishing (9469ecd63). Restated pointwise it still needs: (a) chartLocus (C9); (b) the fibre-restriction of the pic0 class to kappa(t) then to the separable L (my collapse keystones \u2014 but see the diamond wall: the restriction forces a fibre-field k-tower that must be native); (c) the degree/choose-m/kill-h1/greedy-drop(B-1)/density(B-2)/package chain. Pins for the coverage core: degAt_pic0_mul_pow (DegreeSeam:145), degAt_chartValue (C5), exists_bound_subsingleton_hModule_one_of_isFinite_toP1 at L (UniformVanishing:71), exists_effective_sub_h0_eq_one (B-1, CoverageDrop), Over.dense_baseChange_rationalPoints (B-2). B-6 (IsLocallySurjective instance) unchanged \u2014 still divRep-gated.\n\nDEVIATIONS vs worksheet s1.2 step 1: (1) the collapse is stated as map_mk_eq_unit_of_algHom (explicit l + clean tower) rather than an existential-bundled restriction \u2014 forced by the diamond wall; the exists-over-instances form is mathematically fine but un-elaborable with a composite letI. (2) The picEtAffineEquiv/PicEtAff.mk read (worksheet step-1 preamble) is left to the consumer; the collapse operates on a PicEtAff C K element directly.",
