      "body": "P-fib-N consumer seam (found by the PFibPack lane, I-0233): the DD-0 multiplier budget windowS_spec is ONE g SHORT for discharging the pack's tower budget h\u03b2S at a residue field. Binding for the G-4 seed lane (DivSchemeSeedUniv) and the DD-0 owner.\n\nTHE SEAM: at \u03ba(p) the vanishing threshold hvan (\u2200 W, \u03b2 \u2264 deg W \u2192 H\u00b9=0) can only be produced from transported witnesses: peeling (subsingleton_hModule_one_of_witness) from a transported a-exponent window gives \u03b2 = a\u00b7\u03b4 + g (\u03c7_\u03ba = 1 \u2212 g via genus_baseField), with base-level input requiring b \u2264 a\u00b7\u03b4 (windowBound_spec at k). Minimal such a has a\u00b7\u03b4 \u2264 b + \u03b4 \u2212 1. The pack's tower budget h\u03b2S demands \u03b2 + 2g \u2264 s\u00b7\u03b4, i.e. a\u00b7\u03b4 + 3g \u2264 s\u00b7\u03b4; worst case needs b + \u03b4 + 3g \u2212 1 \u2264 s\u00b7\u03b4. But windowS_spec only guarantees b + 2g \u2264 (s\u22121)\u00b7\u03b4, i.e. s\u00b7\u03b4 \u2265 b + \u03b4 + 2g \u2014 short by g \u2212 1. For g \u2265 2 the discharge FAILS with the current ledger constant. (The alternative hvan source \u2014 the bridge subsingleton_hModule_one_of_normalization on subsingleton_h1_windowN_sub \u2014 gives \u03b2 = M\u00b7\u03b4 \u2212 2g, which fails h\u03b2S by a mile since M \u226b s. The descent budget h\u03b2N is NOT affected: windowM_spec's (g+2)(s+1)\u00b7\u03b4 slack absorbs \u03b2 \u2248 b + \u03b4 + g comfortably.)\n\nRECOMMENDED FIX (safe, mechanical, but full-rebuild-expensive): strengthen WindowLedger.windowS_exists / windowS_choice from 'least s with (s\u22121)\u00b7\u03b4 \u2265 b + 2g' to 'least s with (s\u22121)\u00b7\u03b4 \u2265 b + 3g'. This is a monotone strengthening: windowS_spec consumers receive a stronger fact, every downstream theorem goes through the spec (DAT-D discipline rule 1 \u2014 no numeric bounds downstream), so proofs are unaffected; only the VALUES of windowS_choice/windowM_choice shift, forcing a 