of: Module.mem_support_iff_nontrivial_residueField_tensorProduct at pz OVER \u0393(V)\n--        (chartColengthModule_finite, I-0303) + not_nontrivial_iff_subsingleton + TensorProduct.comm.\n--        NO comap to R (that was the fatal 2c error). \u03ba(pz) = the fibre \u03ba(z). Single-point.\n\n(step 2 iii \u2014 the fibre\u2192stalk reduction, pure module algebra)\ntheorem notMem_support_chartColengthModule_of_forall_exists_notMem_mul_read_mem_span\n  (K) (b) (s) [Module.Finite R \u21a5K] {z} (hz : z \u2208 relPinnedChart C R \u03c0 b)\n  (hgen : \u2200 \u2983\u03c8\u2984, \u03c8 \u2208 K \u2192 \u2203 r \u2209 ((isAffineOpen_relPinnedChart C R \u03c0 b).primeIdealOf \u27e8z,hz\u27e9).asIdeal,\n    r * relThetaResSide a b le_rfl \u03c8 \u2208 Ideal.span {relThetaResSide a b le_rfl s}) :\n  (isAffineOpen_relPinnedChart C R \u03c0 b).primeIdealOf \u27e8z,hz\u27e9 \u2209\n    Module.support \u0393(V) \u21a5(chartColengthModule K b s)\n-- proof: Module.notMem_support_iff' (\u2200m \u2203r\u2209pz, r\u2022m=0) over the \u0393(V)-span generators via\n--        submodule closure (pz prime for +, 1\u2209pz for 0).\n\n(the isLocalization_stalk bridge \u2014 reusable, scheme-general)\ntheorem IsAffineOpen.exists_notMem_primeIdealOf_mul_mem_span_singleton_of_germ_mem_span\n  {X : Scheme} {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {z : X} (hz : z \u2208 U) {b x : \u0393(X, U)}\n  (h : (X.presheaf.germ U z hz).hom x \u2208 Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.germ U z hz).hom b}) :\n  \u2203 r \u2209 (hU.primeIdealOf \u27e8z,hz\u27e9).asIdeal, r * x \u2208 Ideal.span {b}\n-- proof: stalk = Localization.AtPrime (isLocalization_stalk, germ = algebraMap via\n--        stalk_open_algebraMap); IsLocalization.surj clears the denominator, map_eq_zero_iff\n--        kills the kernel. This is the fresh isLocalization_stalk wiring I-0302/I-0305 flagged.\n\n(germ-level RD-N reduction \u2014 cleanest achiever target)\ntheorem notMem_support_chartColengthModule_of_forall_germ_mem_span\n  (K)(b)(s)[Module.Finite R \u21a5K]{z}(hz : z \u2208 relPinnedChart C R \u03c0 b)\n  (hgerm : \u2200 \u2983\u03c8\u2984, \u03c8 \u2208 K \u2192 (germ_z).hom (relThetaResSide a b le_rfl \u03c8)\n      \u2208 Ideal.span {(germ_z).hom (relThetaResSide a b le_rfl s)}) :\n  primeIdealOf \u27e8z,hz\u27e9 \u2209 Module.support \u0393(V) \u21a5(chartColengthModule K b s)\n-- = bridge \u2218 step-2(iii).\n\n(the ASSEMBLY \u2014 SeedUnivRDN discharged from seed-level germ divisibility)\ntheorem seedUnivRDN_of_forall_germ_mem_span\n  (hgerm : \u2200 z, \u2200 \u2983\u03c8\u2984, \u03c8 \u2208 divUniversalSeedK \u2026 \u2192\n    germ_z(relThetaResSide (windowM_choice \u03c0 h\u03c0 g) (seedUniv.side z) le_rfl \u03c8)\n      \u2208 Ideal.span {germ_z(relThetaResSide \u2026 (seedUniv.side z) le_rfl (seedUniv.sec z))}) :\n  SeedUnivRDN C h\u03c0 g r\u2081 r\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082 i j hO h\u03c7\n-- proof: per-z notMem_support_\u2026_forall_germ_mem_span at K:=divUniversalSeedK (finite_divUniversalSeedK);\n--        seedUnivColength \u21d4 chartColengthModule defeq closes it.\n\n=== WHAT LANDED vs RESIDUAL ===\nLANDED (\u03ba(z) pivot reduction chain, complete & committed): SeedUnivRDN is now reduced \u2014\nunconditionally bar one honest premise \u2014 to the SINGLE-POINT seed-level germ divisibility\n`\u2200z \u2200\u03c8\u2208K_univ, germ_z(read \u03c8) \u2208 \u27e8germ_z(read sec z)\u27e9`. The dead \u03ba(p) 2c bridge is NOT consumed\n(left intact per I-0305). The degree obstruction (I-0305 \u00a72) never applies: everything is \u03ba(z)\nsingle-point.\n\nRESIDUAL (the genuine remaining geometric wall \u2014 step 2(ii), NOT built):\n1. The germ-divisibility premise itself: from the achiever (I-0291\n   exists_relThetaWindowEquiv_\u2026_achieves_seedPrime, coeffAt=baseDivisorAt at z) prove\n   germ_z(read \u03c8) \u2208 \u27e8germ_z(read sec z)\u27e9. Content = fibre-DVR order comparison\n   (germ_relThetaResSide_dvd_iff_ord_le, DivSchemeUnivFibreHdiv, over \u03ba(p)) + the total-space\n   germ_z (over R_Z) \u2194 fibre germ (over \u03ba(p)) BASE CHANGE. This is the fresh, heavy, multi-piece\n   scheme plumbing I-0302 \u00a72c / I-0305 \u00a7route step 2(i)/(ii) flagged (isLocalization_stalk\n   base-change + reading base change). The single-point isLocalization_stalk half is now landed\n   (the bridge above); the fibre\u2194total germ identification remains.\n2. hfib (I-0305 M): still needs the I-0291 achiever wired into seedUniv.sec (current sec = OLD\n   exists_seedPoint, DivSchemeSeedUnivGen:283) to get uniform windowCompare\u22600; NOT built here.\n\nDOWNSTREAM: once (1)+(2) land \u21d2 SeedUnivRDN + hfib discharged \u21d2 isGenerator_seedUniv'\nunconditional (bar h\u03c7/hO) \u21d2 certificate (non-circular) \u21d2 U1 = divUniversalFamily \u21d2 divRep.\nAnti-circularity preserved: certificate-FREE, IsCertified-FREE, single-point throughout.",
