=kappa(p); identify ker(f_V(X)kappa) with the second window divUniversalSeedK' via ker_baseChangeMkQ_eq_span_windowCompare (Res:207) + divUniversal_carve_residueField (FamilyUniv:135, carvePairArrow=0) + baseChange_carvePairArrow_eq_zero_iff/ker_baseChange_mkQ (DivCarveKit:190/91); the base kernel spans the fibre kernel by the SlicingFlatKernel corank-g pin, which needs the CONSTANT fibre dimension g via finrank_divUniversalFibreKM_add (AssembleKappa:207) \u2014 the function-field window divUniversalFibreKM identification (divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span, Res:376).\nGOTCHA (verified, MEMORY-WORTHY): applying the chart triangle / windowCompare at kappa(p) over a GENERAL test ring needs [Algebra k kappa(p)][IsScalarTower k R kappa(p)] \u2014 the I-0255 residue-field k-tower minefield (RingHom.toAlgebra composite letI => whnf NON-termination even at 1e6 heartbeats). The carve-pin lane must wire these towers NATIVELY (NOT via toAlgebra composites). NEXT LANE: build the fibre-reading bridge (chartReadMap.rTensor kappa(p) transported by relPinnedTermBaseChangeAlg = relThetaResSide of Theta_kappa(windowCompare)) with native kappa(p) towers, then wire the carve + corank.",
