      "body": "hsub carve rank-g BUILD \u2014 landed the missing converse (hinj \u27f9 hsub) completing hsub \u27fa hinj \u27fa hspan; established the anti-circularity blocker precisely. Full hsub does NOT land this session (genuine multi-week XL + a real cycle at the piece level + the unbuilt germ bridge). New file Picard/DivSchemeRedesignHsub.lean (179 L). Single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake build GREEN under the mkdir lock (8673 jobs, my module 41s, peak RSS 6.8 GB). Both keystones lean_verify axiom-clean. Root: HEAD-blob + own line only (sibling PicEtCrossBaseGraph add + Hinj/Achiever/FibreCut/Seed removals in working tree NOT swept; show --stat = my 2 paths, root +1). Zero sorries (Challenge.lean sorries pre-existing).\n\n=== COMMIT (this lane) ===\n- c7020ea4b  DD-4 hsub: carve fibre non-collapse \u27fa induced-map fibre injectivity (hinj \u27f9 hsub)\n\n=== KEYSTONES (VERBATIM; namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaGeneratorSeed; vars {k C R \u03c0 a K} (D : ThetaGeneratorSeed C R \u03c0 a K)) ===\n(1) hsub_of_forall_liftQ_rTensor_injective (D)\n    (hinj : \u2200 (z : relCurve C R)(p : PrimeSpectrum R), Function.Injective (((LinearMap.ker ((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype)).liftQ ((D.kColengthMap z).comp K.subtype) le_rfl).rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField))\n    : \u2200 (z)(p), Function.Injective ((D.sideColengthSubmodule z).subtype.rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField)\n  \u2014 the MISSING CONVERSE: hsub (the exact statement forall_flat_colength_quotient_of_hsub + RD-N consume) FROM the induced-map fibre injectivity hinj. Proof: fbar corestricts to \u0113 : K\u29f8ker f_z \u2243 N z, fbar\u2297\u03ba = (N.subtype\u2297\u03ba)\u2218(\u0113\u2297\u03ba), \u0113\u2297\u03ba surjective; element chase.\n(2) forall_sideColengthSubmodule_subtype_rTensor_injective_iff (D) : hsub \u27fa hinj (packaged from (1) + landed hinj_of_forall_sideColengthSubmodule_subtype_rTensor_injective).\n\nEffect: hsub \u27fa hinj \u27fa hspan is a closed loop. The carve rank-g pin may target the cleanest of the three (f\u0304_z, image = fibre window divUniversalFibreKM, corank g) and still discharge hsub.\n\n=== ANTI-CIRCULARITY FINDING (BINDING \u2014 why the wall stood across I-0284/0286/0290/0292) ===\nA GENUINE DEFINITIONAL CYCLE at the PIECE level. hsub/hinj/hspan mention D.piece z = basicOpen(D.h z) (via kColengthMap) and D.eqn z = read(D.sec z). At the concrete redesigned seedUniv', D.h z is the ann-cutter (DivSchemeRedesignFibreCut), produced by RD-N, which consumes brick-1's Flat(colength z \u29f8 N z) = forall_flat_colength_quotient_of_hsub, which consumes hsub \u2014 so hsub(seedUniv') cannot even be WRITTEN before h z is defined, and h z needs RD-N needs the flat needs hsub. Therefore the piece-level hsub in DivSchemeRedesignJFlat.lean CANNOT be instantiated non-circularly at seedUniv'. RESOLUTION (h z-free, matches I-0289 file-plan + I-0292 pt 3): the carve wiring of hsub must be CHART-lite separable + l : E.Carrier -a[K] L; apply keystone 1/2. The L/K/k tower is a CLEAN instance hypothesis (campaign-idiomatic, cf DivSchemeSeed.lean:73). Well-definedness across splittings = E-iv-alg + ClassCohomology:111 (not re-derived here).\n\nNEW WALL / GOTCHA (verified this pass, MEMORY-WORTHY for B-4/B-5/B-6): the I-0236 two-level-tower diamond is a GENUINE whnf NON-TERMINATION (not merely slow \u2014 still times out at 1,000,000 heartbeats). Instantiating L with a RingHom.toAlgebra composite letI (letI : Algebra k L := ((algebraMap K L).comp (algebraMap k K)).toAlgebra, the DegreeZero.lean:339 pattern) EXPLODES the moment PicEtAff.map C L unfolds the base-changed etale carrier (a MvPolynomial-quotient). This is why the collapse is stated with the tower as CLEAN hypotheses and NOT bundled as an existential over-instances of a cofinality-produced L. degAff_mul survives the same composite letI only because degAff never forms map/baseChange. CONSEQUENCE: B-5 coverage step 1 and B-4 link-2 (etale-carrier image transport) MUST supply the fibre extension L via a NATIVE k-algebra tower (residue-field-based instances), never a composite letI, or they hit this wall. respectTransparency false + maxSynthPendingDepth 3 do NOT fix it.\n\nC9 / divRep BOUNDARY (where B-5 stops, per worksheet): chartLocus is still UNDEFINED (DAT-C C9 unshipped, confirmed I-0252). Therefore COV-1 pic0_chartLocus_cover CANNOT YET BE STATED. Its target predicate is the witness/h1=0 form of Pic0ChartLocusOpen keystone isOpen_setOf_exists_witness_h1_vanishing (9469ecd63). Restated pointwise it still needs: (a) chartLocus (C9); (b) the fibre-restriction of the pic0 class to kappa(t) then to the separable L (my collapse keystones \u2014 but see the diamond wall: the restriction forces a fibre-field k-tower that must be native); (c) the degree/choose-m/kill-h1/greedy-drop(B-1)/density(B-2)/package chain. Pins for the coverage core: degAt_pic0_mul_pow (DegreeSeam:145), degAt_chartValue (C5), exists_bound_subsingleton_hModule_one_of_isFinite_toP1 at L (UniformVanishing:71), exists_effective_sub_h0_eq_one (B-1, CoverageDrop), Over.dense_baseChange_rationalPoints (B-2). B-6 (IsLocallySurjective instance) unchanged \u2014 still divRep-gated.\n\nDEVIATIONS vs worksheet s1.2 step 1: (1) the collapse is stated as map_mk_eq_unit_of_algHom (explicit l + clean tower) rather than an existential-bundled restriction \u2014 forced by the diamond wall; the exists-over-instances form is mathematically fine but un-elaborable with a composite letI. (2) The picEtAffineEquiv/PicEtAff.mk read (worksheet step-1 preamble) is left to the consumer; the collapse operates on a PicEtAff C K element directly.",
