he cleanest of the three (f\u0304_z, image = fibre window divUniversalFibreKM, corank g) and still discharge hsub.\n\n=== ANTI-CIRCULARITY FINDING (BINDING \u2014 why the wall stood across I-0284/0286/0290/0292) ===\nA GENUINE DEFINITIONAL CYCLE at the PIECE level. hsub/hinj/hspan mention D.piece z = basicOpen(D.h z) (via kColengthMap) and D.eqn z = read(D.sec z). At the concrete redesigned seedUniv', D.h z is the ann-cutter (DivSchemeRedesignFibreCut), produced by RD-N, which consumes brick-1's Flat(colength z \u29f8 N z) = forall_flat_colength_quotient_of_hsub, which consumes hsub \u2014 so hsub(seedUniv') cannot even be WRITTEN before h z is defined, and h z needs RD-N needs the flat needs hsub. Therefore the piece-level hsub in DivSchemeRedesignJFlat.lean CANNOT be instantiated non-circularly at seedUniv'. RESOLUTION (h z-free, matches I-0289 file-plan + I-0292 pt 3): the carve wiring of hsub must be CHART-level \u2014 over V = relPinnedChart (side z), le_rfl, base ideal J = \u27e8read \u03c8 : \u03c8\u2208K\u27e9, colength \u0393(V)\u29f8J, N_V = J-image \u2014 which is what RD-N's J-flatness input (iii) actually needs, and which the universal carve (divUniversal_carve_residueField, itself h z-free) supplies. The piece-level statement then follows by localizing to D(h z) \u2286 V AFTER h z is chosen. The pure-linear-algebra equivalences (this file + Hinj) hold at either level; only the carve pin hinj is residual and must be stated chart-level.\n\n=== RESIDUAL \u2014 the genuine XL carve pin, UNCHANGED difficulty ===\nhinj_chart / hsub_chart: at chart V, (K\u29f8ker read_V) \u2297 \u03ba(p) \u2192 (\u0393(V)\u29f8J) \u2297 \u03ba(p) injective because image = divUniversalFibreKM (corank g via finrank_divUniversalFibreKM_add, AssembleKappa:207) and the reading is an ISO onto it (rank pin from divUniversal_carve_residueField, FamilyUniv:135, transported by ker_baseChange_mkQ + baseChange_carvePairArrow_eq_zero_iff, DivCarveKit:91/190). BLOCKER unchanged: the section\u2192functionField germ bridge (relThetaResSide over V \u2194 thetaFieldRead / divFamPhi) is UNBUILT \u2014 needed to see N_V \u2297 \u03ba inside the carve cokernel. Building it at the CHART level (le_rfl) is cleaner than at D(h') and sidesteps the cycle. NEXT LANE: reformulate reading-map/base-ideal/colength/N at the chart (le_rfl), then wire the carve via the germ bridge.",
