eves_seedPrime (brick 2, I-0291), h := the ann-cutter (2). The h field needs, per z, the premise 'z not-in supp(N z)' over Gamma(chart) \u2014 i.e. RD-N. seedUniv'.IsGenerator is then isGenerator_of_ann_cutter (hann from the ann-cutter's smul_eq_zero -> mul-in-span, hfib from the achiever windowCompare!=0 span bridge, exactly as old seedUniv's hfib).\n2. RD-N (read_sec_generates_stalk, spec \u00a71.3): span{read sec z} = J z at stalk O_z, equivalently hV.primeIdealOf z not-in Module.support Gamma(chart) (N z). Inputs: (i) read sec z in J z; (ii) achiever generates J-bar_p at z (brick 2); (iii) J z R_Z-flat (brick 1, forall_flat_colength_quotient_of_hspan, I-0290, but its hsub_seedUniv carve wiring is the UNBUILT XL residual). Proof shape: flat => J cap pGamma = pJ (no Tor_1), J-bar_p = J/pJ, Nakayama over O_z. The k[eps] guard (I-0231) lives here: MUST route through flatness. To feed the fibre-cutter (2), bridge Module.support Gamma(chart) at primeIdealOf z to the stalk O_z via hV.isLocalization_stalk.\n3. hann from smul: the cutter (2) gives 'forall n : N z, h . n = 0' with N z = image of readings mod <read sec z>; that yields 'h z * read psi in <read sec z>' (hann shape of (4)/(5)) once N z is set up as the chart-level sideColengthSubmodule analog (over the chart V, le_rfl, not the piece).",
