      "body": "BPF/no-leak crux (G-4 seed / DD-4 seam): NO-REDESIGN. The current seedUniv section/piece choice CANNOT support the hfield lower bound (hle) or the hcolFin no-leak. DESIGN ESCALATION (seedUniv.sec + seedUniv.h in DivSchemeSeedUnivGen.lean need revision). No Lean written, no sorries, nothing committed \u2014 verdict is analytic, grounded entirely in LANDED lemmas (same discipline as I-0260). The germ bridge (I-0287) did NOT dissolve the wall; it sharpened/moved it but it persists, rooted in the same sec defect as I-0258/I-0260.\n\n=== THE DECISIVE OBSTRUCTION (3 verified facts force NO) ===\n\n(1) The fibre window is HIGH-DIMENSIONAL, never 1-dim. dim_kappa(p) divUniversalFibreKM = h0(O(N)) - g = deg N + 1 - 2g (finrank_divUniversalFibreKM_add, AssembleKappa:207, + h0=degN+1-g via subsingleton_h1_windowN). deg N = M*delta with M*delta >= b + 2g + (g+2)(s+1)delta (windowM_spec WindowLedger:189 + deg_windowN WindowFieldTransport:319). Since delta>=1 and (g+2)(s+1)delta>=2, dim >= 2 robustly (typically much more). So the \"1-dim => trivial span\" YES-escape is CLOSED: readings of K_univ span the whole >=2-dim window (divUniversalFibreKM_eq_span, Res:376), so read(sec) (one element) must DIVIDE a >=2-dim family of readings on D(h').\n\n(2) seedUniv.h z = algebraMap f is a BASE-RING pullback (Gen:289, f in R_Z from exists_forall_windowCompare_ne_zero). By relPinnedSectionsMap_algebraMap_eq (Facts:212), base-change to kappa(p) gives algebraMap(f mod p); for f not-in p (i.e. p in D(f), incl. basePrime(germ_z) and its whole D(f)-nbhd) f mod p != 0 is a UNIT in the field kappa(p), so its basicOpen is top. Hence D(h') = the ENTIRE pinned fibre chart over kappa(p). ZERO FIBREWISE SHRINK ROOM \u2014 the YES-branch escape (\"extra vanishing avoidable by shrinking h z\") is STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE for h z = algebraMap f: it shrinks the base only, never the fibre.\n\n(3) The germ-bridge residual hle (relThetaResSide_mem_span_of_forall_ord_le, DivSchemeUnivFibreHdiv.lean:203-211) needs, with s:=Theta(windowCompare x_psi), t:=Theta(windowCompare x_sec):  for every closed w in D(h'), ord(read psi)_w <= ord(read sec)_w. Upper bound available: ord(read psi)_w <= B_w := divisorBound(windowN - d_p)_w for ALL w (divFamPhi_windowCompare_mem, Res:423 + divUniversalSeedFibreDivisor_spec, Fields:146). So hle <=> read(sec) ACHIEVES the ceiling ord(read sec)_w = B_w at EVERY w of D(h') = the whole chart. But seedUniv.sec z = relThetaWindowEquiv x carries ONLY windowCompare(kappa(p),x) != 0 (Gen:300, exists_sec_windowCompare_ne_zero_seedPrime) = \"read(sec) != 0 as a fibre section\", NO minimal-vanishing/achiever data. A generic nonzero element of H0(windowN - d_p) has deg(windowN - d_p) = deg N - g > 0 EXTRA zeros (moving part) landing generically INSIDE the chart. At any extra-zero w0, ord(read sec)_{w0} < B_{w0} while some psi (readings span the window) hits B_{w0} => hle FAILS. windowCompare!=0 does not even prevent an extra zero AT z itself.\n\n=== SAME defect kills hcolFin (no-leak) ===\npiece z = D(h z), eqn z = read(sec) (Family:93,113). no-leak = closure(piece cap V(read sec)) subset piece. With h = base pullback, piece = chart cap phi^-1(D(f)) (whole fibre over D(f)); read(sec)'s relative zero locus leaks to special fibres over boundary of D(f) \u2014 EXACTLY I-0285's toy counterexample (P1/k[t], {x=t}, piece D(t): trace leaks to (0,0) not in piece, colength k[t,1/t] not R-finite). windowCompare!=0 (fibrewise nonvanishing) is insufficient, as I-0285 already found. hfield and hcolFin share the root cause.\n\n=== WHY the germ bridge (I-0287) did NOT save it ===\nIt reduced the RELATIVE hfield to a FIBREWISE ord inequality \u2014 genuine progress that sidesteps I-0260's \"fibrewise-does-not-lift-to-relative\" objection (that content now lives in the flatness/carve clauses hcolFlat/hspan). But the fibrewise inequality STILL demands read(sec) be a fibre BPF-achiever, and because D(h')=whole chart it means achievement on the ENTIRE chart. The wall moved (relative-generation -> fibrewise-achievement-on-the-whole-chart) but persists.\n\n=== WHAT seedUniv MUST BECOME (the redesign, orchestrator matter) ===\nBOTH pointwise fields need revision (currently sec=windowCompare!=0 lift, h=algebraMap base-pullback):\n (A) sec z := a RELATIVE ACHIEVER in K_univ=divUniversalSeedK whose kappa(p)-fibre reading achieves the base divisor bd=d_p at z (field-level per-point achiever exists_coeffAt_eq_baseDivisorAt, BaseDivisor:143, LIFTED to a relative R_Z-section inside K_univ) \u2014 so z is NOT an extra zero. This achiever-lift is I-0258's flagged generally-NON-liftable step (a single R_Z window vector need not reduce to a chosen kappa(p)-combination f; windowCompare(W) is only an R_Z/p-semilinear image whose kappa(p)-span, not itself, is the window). It is the DD-4 base-field-transport / relative-BPF seam I-0260 recommended (DivSchemeFamily:44); FIELD-level BPF infra (BpfSpan, BaseDivisorSpan) has NO relative/R_Z version.\n (B) h z := a genuine CURVE section cutting a fibre-neighbourhood of z (NOT algebraMap of a base element), so D(h') shrinks in the fibre to a punctured nbhd of z that excludes read(sec)'s OTHER extra zeros. Only then does read(sec) meet B_w on all of D(h'), giving hle; and V(eqn z)=d_p's branch through z becomes proper/contained, giving hcolFin.\n\n=== STATUS ===\nhdiv_seedUniv / seedUniv_hfield / hnoleak_seedUniv: NONE present (grep-confirmed absent), NONE landed \u2014 correctly so; a bridge-sec seed would BAKE IN a sec for which hle/hcolFin are unprovable. Germ bridge (15d9eb465) + shared brick (2b6b00cf5) + hcolFin reduction (4ec2a0d60/819f9dbc2) remain valid and forward-compatible \u2014 they consume WHATEVER sec the redesign produces. The ONE pointwise residual (hle at every closed w of D(h')) is now razor-isolated; discharged the instant seedUniv.sec becomes a relative achiever and seedUniv.h a fibre-cutter. Verdict: the seed does NOT close with the current construction. Escalate the achiever-lift / relative-BPF seam.",
