      "body": "DAT-C C4 PARTIAL \u2014 Nakayama local-basis companion + local-rescaling corollary + N4 LANDED (the mono-engine module heart); N5 relative-uniqueness + the \u00a73.2 chart mono (base-twist coset) DEFERRED with pinned seams.\n\nCommit fc34504941498bfe8ed925f1bb61c511e96a5874 (parent 22cd53efb). AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyMonoH1.lean, 195 L. Private-index CAS; root = HEAD blob + only my import line (sibling PicEtCrossBaseGraph uncommitted line NOT swept, protocol \u00a74b). Single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake build GREEN under the mkdir lock (8866 jobs, 10s). Zero sorries; zero new warnings. lean_verify: all three keystones axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].\n\nKEYSTONES (verbatim):\n\n- Module.exists_notMem_bijective_toSpanSingleton {B Q} [CommRing B] [AddCommGroup Q] [Module B Q] [Module.Finite B Q] [Module.Projective B Q] (p : PrimeSpectrum B) (hrank : Module.rankAtStalk Q p = 1) (q : Q) (hq : (q \u2297\u209c[B] (1 : p.asIdeal.ResidueField) : Q \u2297[B] p.asIdeal.ResidueField) \u2260 0) : \u2203 f : B, f \u2209 p.asIdeal \u2227 Function.Bijective (LocalizedModule.map (Submonoid.powers f) (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton B Q q))\n  \u2014 THE DEFERRED GAP-3 companion (I-0253 (4)): a GIVEN fibrewise-nonzero element of a rank-1 finite projective module is a Zariski-local BASIS. Over the local stalk R\u209a, Q\u209a is free rank 1 (free_of_flat_of_isLocalRing); basisUnique b; fibre nonzeroness transported via (LocalizedModule.equivTensorProduct).lTensor \u2218 AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange (\u03ba\u2297R\u209a Q\u209a \u2245 \u03ba\u2297B Q, 1\u2297mkq\u21a61\u2297q) pins coord c to a unit; mkq spans; Module.Invertible R\u209a Q\u209a (nonempty_linearEquiv_of_finrank_eq_one + Invertible.congr) + Module.Invertible.bijective_of_surjective \u27f9 bijection; Module.FinitePresentation.exists_notMem_bijective spreads to D(f). Stalk map identified with toSpanSingleton over R\u209a via IsLocalizedModule.ext.\n\n- Module.exists_notMem_smul_eq_of_tmul_ne_zero (same hyps + q' : Q) : \u2203 f \u2209 p.asIdeal, \u2203 a : Localization.Away f, (LocalizedModule.mk q' 1 : LocalizedModule.Away f Q) = a \u2022 LocalizedModule.mk q 1\n  \u2014 local-rescaling corollary (N5 engine input): a second element lies in the B_f-span of the local basis.\n\n- AlgebraicGeometry.CertifiedDivisorFamily.picClass_sectionLocalEquationsOfFibrewiseRegular [IsNoetherianRing S] (G : CertifiedDivisorFamily C S \u03c0 n) (s : \u21a5(gluedSubmodule S G.adaptation.divisorDatum.pieces G.adaptation.divisorDatum.unit \u22a4)) (hfib : \u2200 j p, Function.Injective ((Scheme.mulSectionEnd S (G.adaptation.divisorDatum.component s j)).rTensor p.asIdeal.ResidueField)) : (G.adaptation.divisorDatum.sectionLocalEquationsOfFibrewiseRegular s hfib).picClass = G.eqns.picClass\n  \u2014 N4 (DAT-A on the nose): any fibrewise-regular section of D_G cuts a LocalEquations family of \u010cech class G.eqns.picClass. (sectionLocalEquationsOfFibrewiseRegular_picClass + C0 cechPicClass_divisorDatum.)\n\nDEVIATIONS: (1) Companion output is the bijective form matching mathlib v4.31 exists_notMem_bijective. (2) The \"a is a UNIT when q' is fibrewise nonzero on D(f)\" strengthening is NOT built (easy addendum). (3) mathlib v4.31 has NO \"rank-1 finite projective \u27f9 Module.Invertible\" theorem; I obtain Module.Invertible only at the local stalk R\u209a (free rank 1 \u27f9 invertible), sufficient for the stalk step.\n\nN5 (relative DivEq uniqueness) \u2014 NOT LANDED, SEAM PINNED: given fibrewise-nonzero \u03c3,\u03c3' \u2208 H\u2070(D_G) (generators at every prime \u2014 C2 exists_fibrewise_generator_divisorDatum), cover Spec S by companion D(f_i), get \u03c3'=a_i\u00b7\u03c3 (corollary) with a_i\u2208(S_{f_i})\u02e3 (STRENGTHEN corollary: fibrewise-nonzero \u27f9 in no prime \u27f9 unit), rescale \u27f9 DivEq (DivisorFamily.lean:73 DivEq = common-refinement+pointwise-unit; DivisorClass rescale/picClass_rescale :413/:450 \u2014 need divEq_rescale, n