      "body": "CHART-U(b) partial \u2014 datum-level witness-locus openness + transport(ii) topological half LANDED (fresh start, predecessor died in survey)\n\nFILE: MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0ChartLocusOpen.lean (137 L). Commits: 9469ecd63 (core), 461da4972 (transport). Root-wired (HEAD-blob + only my line, protocol s4). Zero sorries; every keystone axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; single-module LEAN_NUM_THREADS=1 lake green under mkdir lock (8864 jobs); zero warnings in my file.\n\nKEYSTONE 1 (verbatim) \u2014 the datum-level heart of CHART-U(b), engine-open in the chartLocus witness form:\ntheorem BasicOpenCocycleDatum.isOpen_setOf_exists_witness_h1_vanishing (D : BasicOpenCocycleDatum C B \u03c0) (h\u03c0 : \u03c0 \u226b P1.structureMap k = C.hom) : IsOpen {q : PrimeSpectrum B | \u2203 W : ((C \u2297 overSpec k q.asIdeal.ResidueField).left).CurveDivisor, Scheme.CurveDivisor.picClass q.asIdeal.ResidueField W = Scheme.CechPic.map (relCurveMap C B q.asIdeal.ResidueField) D.cechPicClass \u2227 Subsingleton (Sheaf.HModule ((C \u2297 overSpec k q.asIdeal.ResidueField).left.divisorSheaf q.asIdeal.ResidueField W) 1)}\nProof = datumRigidEngine_isOpen_vanishing (Noetherian-free engine, dat-d s3.5) read through C1's two-way dictionary BasicOpenCocycleDatum.subsingleton_h1_tensor_iff_exists_witness (GAP-6): the engine complex-form fibre cond Subsingleton(H1(pair D) \u2297[B] \u03ba(q)) is pointwise the effective-witness/h1=0 cond. Class-intrinsic. Context: [IsFinite \u03c0][SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 C.hom][IsProper C.hom][GeometricallyIrreducible C.hom].\n\nKEYSTONE 2/3 (verbatim) \u2014 CHART-U(b) transport (ii) topological half, the 'one IsOpenMap application' of w4-datb s1.6:\ntheorem isOpen_of_isOpen_preimage_of_isOpenMap_surjective {X Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y] {f : X \u2192 Y} (hcont : Continuous f) (hopen : IsOpenMap f) (hsurj : Function.Surjective f) {V : Set Y} (hV : IsOpen (f \u207b\u00b9' V)) : IsOpen V\ntheorem isOpen_of_isOpen_comap_preimage {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (f : R \u2192+* S) (hopen : IsOpenMap (PrimeSpectrum.comap f)) (hsurj : Function.Surjective (PrimeSpectrum.comap f)) {V : Set (PrimeSpectrum R)} (hV : IsOpen (PrimeSpectrum.comap f \u207b\u00b9' V)) : IsOpen V\nProof = mathlib IsOpenMap.isQuotientMap + IsQuotientMap.isOpen_preimage (+ PrimeSpectrum.continuous_comap).\n\nAMENDMENT COMPLIANCE (I-0248 / I-0251): built against the DAT-C frozen interface AS AMENDED. (a-amendment, split predicate for arbitrary plus classes): honored \u2014 the witness locus is stated in the effective-witness/h1=0 (dimension/witness) form; no reliance on chartValue-collapse, so it covers arbitrary plus classes. (b-amendment, pinned openness chain): the chain is realized as pinned \u2014 extraction\u2192(shifted datum)\u2192RE-5-free engine (C1 made the engine Noetherian-free, so the RE-5/transport-(i) descent is OBVIATED for openness; recorded) \u2192 witness-form openness (keystone 1) \u2192 transport (ii) topological (keystones 2/3). NOTE for orchestrator: the C1 landing made datumRigidEngine_isOpen_vanishing Noetherian-free, so transport (i) (Spec B\u2192Spec B0 RE-5 preimage) is NOT needed on the openness path \u2014 one fewer unlanded link than the worksheet chain lists.\n\nREMAINING GAPS (the wall \u2014 two links, honest): (1) the shifted-datum CONSTRUCTOR's class arithmetic: form the honest carrier class c=\u03bb|_B collapse (picEtAffineEquiv\u2192PicEtAff.mk E x\u2192\u00e9tale field-cofinality), then the shifted CechPic c\u00b7\u03b8^m\u00b7[\u03a3]\u207b\u00b9 (theta layer cechPicClass_thetaChartDatum + C0 GAP-1 inverse datum DivisorAdaptation.divisorDatum/.inv), then extract via exists_cechPicClass_eq to instantiate keystone 1's D. The class-multiply-and-extract shell is a thin wrapper over exists_cechPicClass_eq; the genuine content is the \u03a3/\u03b8 naturality proving the datum's fibre class at \u03ba(t) equals \u03bb_t\u00b7\u03b8^m\u00b7(\u2212\u03a3) \u2014 DAT-C-owned vocab (chartValue, ThetaShift), risk of getting the shift wrong is why it is left as a pinned wall not a guess. (2) transport (ii) HARD half \u2014 the fibre-field invariance identifying (PrimeSpectrum.comap f)\u207b\u00b9(chartLocus over A) = chartLocus over the \u00e9tale carrier B: \u03ba(q)/\u03ba(p) separable \u27f9 h1-vanishing of the fibre class is preserved; landed avatar for the AWAY case is C1's DivFamZar.isH1VanishingAt_comap_away_iff \u2014 the general \u00e9tale-carrier analogue is the residue-field base-change seam (H1BaseFieldInvariance is imported/available). Plus: chartLocus itself is not yet DEFINED (DAT-C C9 unshipped) \u2014 B-4's a-amendment split predicate should be the definition; I did not define it to avoid a wrong freeze before C9 lands.\n\nNOTES FOR C9 (DAT-C) consumer: to assemble isOpen_chartLocus, reduce openness on the test T to affine opens Spec A (openness is local, mathlib), collapse \u03bb|_A to PicEtAff.mk E x on the \u00e9tale carrier B=E.Carrier, apply the shifted-datum constructor to get D over B, invoke KEYSTONE 1 for the open witness locus over Spec B, then KEYSTONE 3 (isOpen_of_isOpen_comap_preimage) with f = A\u2192B to push it to Spec A after discharging the fibre-field-invariance preimage identity (gap 2). Etale \u27f9 IsOpenMap(comap) + surjective(cover) supply hopen/hsurj. Transition opens between charts are 01JJ's (no brick).\nNOTES FOR B-5 (DAT-B coverage): the split-predicate collapse lemma (plus class\u2192honest class over finite separable L; w4-datb s6 risk) is SHARED with B-4's gap-1 collapse \u2014 state it once as a named lemma with a characterizing property (DegreeSeam.lean:67-107 template); both consume it. B-5's pointwise cover pic0_chartLocus_cover targets the same witness/h1=0 predicate keystone 1 opens over.",
