      "body": "**Concurrency incidents from the 2026-07-16 evening continuation wave (5 parallel lanes) \u2014 protocol fixes recommended**\n\n1. **Shared-index commit race (SERIOUS, caused transient data loss in HEAD).** All lanes commit through one `workspace.git` index; G-D8's `6197c9676` interleaved with DAT-1's commits and recorded spurious DELETIONS of DAT-1's two freshly-committed files (862 lines vanished from HEAD; byte-identical restore in `a640fef5b`). **Recommended house protocol for concurrent lanes:** commit via a private index \u2014 `GIT_INDEX_FILE=$(mktemp)` + `read-tree HEAD` + add only your paths + `write-tree`/`commit-tree` + compare-and-swap `update-ref` (G-D8's final commit used exactly this and it was clean) \u2014 and always verify `git show --stat HEAD` afterward touches only intended paths.\n\n2. **Stale mutex FILE deadlock.** An agent killed by the 15:18 session limit left `/tmp/claude-1001/ajcr-locks/lake.lock` as a 0-byte FILE; the documented mkdir acquire spins forever against a file, so every lane deadlocked at its build step until the human deleted it (~19:10). Recommendation: the acquire loop should detect a lock that is a plain FILE (protocol violation by definition \u2014 mkdir creates directories) and report it as stale immediately rather than waiting.\n\n3. **/tmp quota outage (~19:00\u201319:20).** uid-1001 tmpfs quota exhaustion (EDQUOT) bricked every Bash call machine-wide, mid-build for several lanes; recovered after human cleanup. Watch /tmp usage when >3 lanes run concurrently.\n\n4. **Foreign-workspace mutex abuse.** An OpenGA-Horizon (Evans) agent held the AJCR lock path for its own `lake cache get` for ~25 min. The AJCR mutex is for AJCR lake invocations only; cross-workspace squatting silently serializes our lanes against unrelated work.\n\nContext: incidents observed and worked around by the five continuation lanes (DD-0, DAT-1, G-D8 closed; DAT-6, DD-F in flight); full details in the lane reports quoted in the respective commit messages.",
